'''Claire Elise Boucher'''<!-- Grimes has not officially changed her name yet. Please do not amend the legal name listed in the article yet. See WP:NAMECHANGES. --> ({{IPAc-en|b|uː|ˈ|ʃ|eɪ}};<ref name="tvmcgill">{{cite web|url=http://www.tvmcgill.com/2011/01/18/on-display-claire-boucher/|title=On Display: Claire Boucher|work=[[McGill University|TVMcGill]]|date=January 18, 2011|access-date=June 7, 2011|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110315030054/http://www.tvmcgill.com/2011/01/18/on-display-claire-boucher/|archive-date=March 15, 2011|url-status=dead}}</ref> born March 17, 1988), known professionally as '''Grimes''', is a Canadian musician, singer, songwriter, and record producer. Her lyrics often touch on [[science fiction]] and [[feminist]] themes. The visuals in her videos are elaborate and sometimes have [[fantasy]] themes. She has released five studio albums.

Born and raised in [[Vancouver]], Grimes began releasing music independently after moving to [[Montreal]] in 2006. She released two albums, ''[[Geidi Primes]]'' and ''[[Halfaxa]]'', in 2010 on [[Arbutus Records]], before signing with [[4AD]] and rising to prominence with the release of her 2012 album, ''[[Visions (Grimes album)|Visions]]''. The album received the Canadian music industry [[Juno Award]] for Electronic Album of the Year, and yielded two singles: "[[Genesis (Grimes song)|Genesis]]" and "[[Oblivion (Grimes song)|Oblivion]]". Following this, her fourth studio album, ''[[Art Angels]]'', was released in 2015, and several publications named it the best album of the year. Her fifth studio album, ''[[Miss Anthropocene]]'', was released in 2020.

Outside of music, Grimes had a voice role in the 2020 action role-playing video game ''[[Cyberpunk 2077]]'' and was a judge on the music competition game show ''[[Alter Ego (TV series)|Alter Ego]]''. She has three children with [[Elon Musk]].

==Early life==
Grimes was born Claire Elise Boucher in [[Vancouver]], British Columbia,<ref name=straight1>{{cite web|first=Gregory|last=Adams|url=https://www.straight.com/article-394584/vancouver/sound-says-most-grimes|title=Sound says most to Grimes|work=Straight|date=May 25, 2011|access-date=July 22, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170912191816/https://www.straight.com/article-394584/vancouver/sound-says-most-grimes|archive-date=September 12, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref> on March 17, 1988,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://vancouversun.com/entertainment/music/five-things-to-know-about-grimes-the-vancouver-pop-star-dating-elon-musk|title=Five Things to Know about Grimes, the Vancouver pop star dating Elon Musk|work=[[Vancouver Sun]]|date=May 9, 2018}}</ref> the first child of Sandy Garossino, a former Crown prosecutor and arts advocate,<ref>{{Cite web|first=Marsha|last=Lederman|url=https://www.theglobeandmail.com/arts/music/claire-boucher-as-grimes-the-coolest-girl-in-canada/article4450330|title=Claire Boucher as Grimes: the coolest girl in Canada|work=[[The Globe and Mail]]|date=July 30, 2012|access-date=August 29, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121129210948/http://www.theglobeandmail.com/arts/music/claire-boucher-as-grimes-the-coolest-girl-in-canada/article4450330|archive-date=November 29, 2012|url-status=live}}</ref> and Maurice Boucher, a former banker who works "in the business side of biotech".<ref>{{Cite magazine|first=Rachel|last=Syme|url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-features/grimes-the-triumph-of-a-self-made-oddball-40059|title=Grimes: The Triumph of a Self-Made Oddball|magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]|date=November 5, 2015|access-date=July 23, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220428040901/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-features/grimes-the-triumph-of-a-self-made-oddball-40059|archive-date=April 28, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Chitra|last=Ramaswamy|url=https://www.scotsman.com/arts-and-culture/music/interview-claire-boucher-musician-1-2277532|title=Interview: Claire Boucher, musician|work=The Scotsman|date=May 6, 2012|access-date=July 23, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200101030605/https://www.scotsman.com/arts-and-culture/music/interview-claire-boucher-musician-1-2277532|archive-date=January 1, 2020|url-status=dead}}</ref> She is of [[French Canadian]] ([[Québécois people|Québécois]]), [[Ukraine|Ukrainian]], and Italian descent.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p95HVaMTZ80|title=Grimes on Sur Le Vif, interviewed by Fanny Lefort ('oldish')|publisher=YouTube|date=May 5, 2012|access-date=December 27, 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140517124234/http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p95HVaMTZ80|archive-date=May 17, 2014|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|first=Alan|last=Brunet|url=https://www.lapresse.ca/arts/musique/entrevues/201203/03/01-4502127-grimes-au-dela-de-limpact-souterrain.php|title=Grimes: au-delà de l'impact souterrain|language=fr|newspaper=[[La Presse (Canadian newspaper)|La Presse]]|date=2014|access-date=October 30, 2019|archive-date=June 3, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220603110952/https://www.lapresse.ca/arts/musique/entrevues/201203/03/01-4502127-grimes-au-dela-de-limpact-souterrain.php|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=glassberg>{{cite web|first=Rachel|last=Glassberg|url=http://www.exberliner.com/articles/six-questions-for-grimes|title=Six Questions for... Grimes|work=[[Exberliner]]|date=May 18, 2012|access-date=January 22, 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200611002806/https://www.exberliner.com/whats-on/music-nightlife/six-questions-for-grimes|archive-date=June 11, 2020|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1H97woq_XM0 |title=Grimes ou l'anti pop / Tout Le Monde En Parle |publisher=YouTube |date=December 1, 2015 |access-date=October 15, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160317154100/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1H97woq_XM0 |archive-date=March 17, 2016 |url-status=live }}</ref> Her grandmother was from [[Ukraine]] and immigrated to [[Canada]].<ref name=glassberg/>

Grimes and her younger brother, Mac, were raised [[Catholic Church|Roman Catholic]], and attended Catholic school in Vancouver.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K8JcROFOVT0|work=Intro Magazin|title=Interview: Intro trifft Grimes|date=September 8, 2012|access-date=February 12, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170214000305/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K8JcROFOVT0|archive-date=February 14, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="vanityfair surrogate">{{cite magazine|first=Devin|last=Gordon|url=https://www.vanityfair.com/style/2022/03/grimes-cover-story-on-music-and-mars|title="Infamy Is Kind Of Fun": Grimes on Music, Mars, and—Surprise!—Her Secret New Baby With Elon Musk|magazine=[[Vanity Fair (magazine)|Vanity Fair]]|date=March 10, 2022|access-date=March 10, 2022|archive-date=May 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220521235459/https://www.vanityfair.com/style/2022/03/grimes-cover-story-on-music-and-mars|url-status=live}}</ref> She later commented that her religious upbringing had a significant impact on her: "It totally influences everything I do. I think I have serious latent Catholic guilt issues."<ref>{{cite web|first=Holly|last=Williams|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/music/features/grimes-hooded-and-booted-8119923.html|title=Grimes: Hooded and booted|work=[[The Independent]]|date=September 10, 2012|access-date=February 13, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231202183437/https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/music/features/grimes-hooded-and-booted-8119923.html|archive-date=December 2, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> Her parents divorced when she was 11 years old, after which her mother remarried.<ref name=gordon>{{cite magazine|first=Devin|last=Gordon|url=https://www.vanityfair.com/style/2022/03/grimes-cover-story-on-music-and-mars|magazine=[[Vanity Fair (magazine)|Vanity Fair]]|title="Infamy Is Kind Of Fun": Grimes on Music, Mars, and Her Secret New Baby With Elon Musk|date=March 10, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230304112358/https://www.vanityfair.com/style/2022/03/grimes-cover-story-on-music-and-mars|archive-date=March 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> Her step-father is an [[Indian Canadians|Indo-Canadian]] man named Ravi Sidhoo, allowing her to experience a multicultural upbringing.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.tribuneindia.com/news/top-headlines/my-stepdads-indian-amid-growing-racism-elon-musks-ex-girlfriend-shares-her-half-indian-roots/|title='My stepdad's Indian': Amid growing racism, Elon Musk's ex-girlfriend shares her half-Indian roots|newspaper=[[The Tribune (India)|The Tribune]]|date=December 31, 2024|access-date=June 17, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250128063407/https://www.tribuneindia.com/news/top-headlines/my-stepdads-indian-amid-growing-racism-elon-musks-ex-girlfriend-shares-her-half-indian-roots/|archive-date=January 28, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> Through her mother's remarriage, she has two stepbrothers, one of whom is a member of the hip hop duo [[LNDN DRGS]] and performs under the name Jay Worthy.<ref>{{cite web|first=Lauren|last=Schwartzberg|url=https://www.complex.com/pigeons-and-planes/2014/06/jay-worthy-lndn-drgs-interview|title=Interview: Jay Worthy on LNDN DRGS, Compton, and Doing Things Differently|work=[[Complex (website)|Complex]]|date=June 4, 2014|access-date=February 13, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022855/https://www.complex.com/pigeons-and-planes/2014/06/jay-worthy-lndn-drgs-interview|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>

In 2006, Grimes graduated from [[Lord Byng Secondary School]] and relocated from Vancouver to [[Montreal]] to attend [[McGill University]]'s joint Bachelor of Arts and Science program. "I was studying general Arts and Science degree, but I was in the electro-acoustics program" she said in early interviews.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.interviewmagazine.com/music/grimes-claire-boucher|title=Grimes of the Heart|magazine=Interview Magazine|date=May 23, 2011|access-date=December 2, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230325210156/https://www.interviewmagazine.com/music/grimes-claire-boucher|archive-date=March 25, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.npr.org/2016/04/27/455769676/feeling-this-a-conversation-with-grimes|title=Feeling This: A Conversation With Grimes|work=[[NPR]]|date=April 27, 2016|access-date=December 2, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022858/https://www.npr.org/2016/04/27/455769676/feeling-this-a-conversation-with-grimes|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> However, she later claimed to have studied neuroscience.<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Sam|last=Walton|url=https://www.loudandquiet.com/interview/grimes-claire-boucher-insists-anyone-can-true/|title=Grimes: Claire Boucher insists that anyone can do what she does. If only it were true|magazine=[[Loud and Quiet]]|date=February 26, 2012|access-date=March 30, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230930041331/https://www.loudandquiet.com/interview/grimes-claire-boucher-insists-anyone-can-true/|archive-date=September 30, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|first=Jon|last=Blistein|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/all-eyes-on-grimes-with-4ad-debut-visions-504516/|title=All Eyes on Grimes With 4AD Debut 'Visions'|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|date=February 21, 2012|access-date=December 2, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230717011942/https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/all-eyes-on-grimes-with-4ad-debut-visions-504516/|archive-date=July 17, 2023|url-status=dead}}</ref> She was expelled in December 2010 for skipping classes.<ref>{{cite web|first=Carrie|last=Battan|url=https://pitchfork.com/features/rising/8689-grimes/|title=Grimes|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=October 17, 2011|access-date=February 13, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240121123745/https://pitchfork.com/features/rising/8689-grimes/|archive-date=January 21, 2024|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Francois|last=Marchand|url=http://www.edmontonjournal.com/entertainment/dirty+grimes+brink+stardom/6171143/story.html|title=Dirty Pop: Grimes on Brink of Stardom|work=[[Edmonton Journal]]|date=February 17, 2012|access-date=July 23, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200918200006/http://www.edmontonjournal.com/entertainment/dirty+grimes+brink+stardom/6171143/story.html|archive-date=September 18, 2020|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|first=Emilie|last=Friedlander|url=http://www.thefader.com/2015/07/28/grimes-cover-story-interview|title=Grimes In Reality|magazine=[[The Fader]]|date=July 28, 2015|access-date=July 22, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170403100818/http://www.thefader.com/2015/07/28/grimes-cover-story-interview|archive-date=April 3, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref>

==Career==
===2009–2011: Career beginnings, ''Geidi Primes'', and ''Halfaxa''===
{{Main|Geidi Primes|Halfaxa|l1=''Geidi Primes''|l2=''Halfaxa''}}

According to the year her original [[Myspace]] account was created, she began writing music under the name Grimes in 2007.<ref name="economictimesindiatimes">{{cite web|url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/magazines/panache/tesla-ceo-elon-musks-girlfriend-grimes-tests-positive-for-covid-19/articleshow/80208179.cms?from=mdr|title=Elon Musk's girlfriend Grimes says she 'finally' has Covid-19|work=[[The Economic Times]]|date=January 11, 2021|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022854/https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/magazines/panache/tesla-ceo-elon-musks-girlfriend-grimes-tests-positive-for-covid-19/articleshow/80208179.cms?from=mdr|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> Her performer name was chosen because at the time, MySpace allowed artists to list three musical genres. She listed "grime" for all three, without knowing what the [[Grime (music genre)|grime music genre]] was.<ref name="seanmichaels">{{cite web|first=Sean|last=Michaels|url=https://www.theguardian.com/music/2014/dec/22/grimes-admits-moniker-grime-genre-option-myspace|title=Grimes admits lifting moniker from grime genre option on Myspace|work=[[The Guardian]]|date=December 22, 2014|access-date=May 8, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150524175427/http://www.theguardian.com/music/2014/dec/22/grimes-admits-moniker-grime-genre-option-myspace|archive-date=May 24, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref> Grimes was self-taught in music and visual art.<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Rachel|last=Syme|url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/features/grimes-the-triumph-of-a-self-made-oddball-20151105|title=Grimes: The Triumph of a Self-Made Oddball|magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]|date=November 5, 2015|access-date=July 23, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170820040853/http://www.rollingstone.com/music/features/grimes-the-triumph-of-a-self-made-oddball-20151105|archive-date=August 20, 2017|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|first=Celia|last=Ellenberg|url=http://www.vogue.com/article/grimes-art-angels-album-hair-color-purple-beauty-makeup-personal-style|title=Grimes On Her New Scene-Stealing Look—And Why Instagram is Killing Her Hair Color Vibe|magazine=[[Vogue (magazine)|Vogue]]|date=November 2, 2015|access-date=August 23, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170823203901/http://www.vogue.com/article/grimes-art-angels-album-hair-color-purple-beauty-makeup-personal-style|archive-date=August 23, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref>

[[File:Grimes at SxSW 2012 (cropped).jpg|thumb|left|upright|Grimes performing at [[South by Southwest]] 2012]]

In January 2010, Grimes released her debut album, ''[[Geidi Primes]]'',<ref name="vulture Geidi Primes">{{cite web|first=Larry|last=Fitzmaurice|url=https://www.vulture.com/2018/12/grimes-the-complete-timeline-so-far.html|title=Grimes: The Complete Timeline (So Far)|work=[[Vulture (blog)|Vulture]]|date=December 3, 2018|access-date=July 23, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220112185111/https://www.vulture.com/2018/12/grimes-the-complete-timeline-so-far.html|archive-date=January 12, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref> a concept album inspired by the ''[[Dune (franchise)|Dune]]'' series,<ref name="vulture Geidi Primes"/><ref>{{cite web|first=Lindsay|last=Zoladz|url=https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/15751-geidi-primes|title=Grimes: Geidi Primes|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=September 7, 2011|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110925092859/http://www.pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/15751-geidi-primes/|archive-date=September 25, 2011|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="earbuddy">{{cite web|first=Gabe|last=McBride|url=http://www.earbuddy.net/871/grimes-geidi-primes-review.html/reviews|title=Grimes – ''Geidi Primes''|work=Earbuddy|date=October 3, 2011|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230408020931/http://www.earbuddy.net/871/grimes-geidi-primes-review.html/reviews|archive-date=April 8, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> followed by her second album, ''[[Halfaxa]]'', in October of the same year.<ref>{{cite web|first=Quinn|last=Moreland|url=https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/21775-halfaxa|title=Halfaxa Grimes|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=April 6, 2016|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230201202020/https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/21775-halfaxa/|archive-date=February 1, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> After the release of ''Halfaxa'', she began to publicly promote her music and tour beyond Montreal. In 2011 Grimes released five songs on her side of the split [[12"]] with [[d'Eon (musician)|d'Eon]], ''[[Darkbloom (EP)|Darkbloom]]'' (through both [[Arbutus Records|Arbutus]] and [[Hippos in Tanks]]).<ref name="Pitchfork genres">{{cite web|first=Lindsay|last=Zoladz|url=http://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/15439-darkbloom-ep|title=d'Eon / Grimes: Darkbloom EP|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=May 19, 2011|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230405182210/https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/15439-darkbloom-ep/|archive-date=April 5, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Alex|last=Hudson|url=https://exclaim.ca/music/article/grimes_deon_team_up_for_split_twelve-inch|title=Grimes and d'Eon Team Up for Split Twelve-Inch|work=[[Exclaim!]]|date=March 3, 2011|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022854/https://exclaim.ca/music/article/grimes_deon_team_up_for_split_twelve-inch|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> Beginning in May 2011, Grimes opened for [[Lykke Li]] on her North American Tour, and the following August her debut album was re-released through No Pain in Pop Records, in CD and vinyl format for the first time.<ref name="Lykke Li tour">{{cite magazine|first=Greg|last=Dybec|url=https://imposemagazine.com/bytes/news/grimes-to-tour-with-lykke-li|title=Grimes to tour with Lykke Li|magazine=[[Impose (magazine)|Impose]]|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406064437/https://imposemagazine.com/bytes/news/grimes-to-tour-with-lykke-li|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Lykke Li tour2">{{cite web|first=Brian|last=Riewer|url=http://sunonthesand.com/2011/grimes-set-to-re-release-debut-album-geidi-primes|title=Grimes Set To Re-Release Debut Album|work=Sun on the Sand|date=July 12, 2011|access-date=February 19, 2012|archive-url=https://archive.today/20120715094551/http://sunonthesand.com/2011/grimes-set-to-re-release-debut-album-geidi-primes|archive-date=July 15, 2012|url-status=dead}}</ref> In 2011, she collaborated with DJ/producer [[BloodPop|Blood Diamonds]].<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Andrew|last=Weatherall|url=http://dummymag.com/mixes/2011/07/07/dummy-mix-79-blood-diamonds|title=Dummy Mix 79 // Blood Diamonds|magazine=Dummy Mag|date=July 7, 2011|access-date=February 22, 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120113192601/http://www.dummymag.com/mixes/2011/07/07/dummy-mix-79-blood-diamonds|archive-date=January 13, 2012|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://thecreatorsproject.com/blog/siren-seduction-qa-with-electronic-musician-grimes|title=Siren Seduction: Q&A With Electronic Musician Grimes|work=The Creator's Profect|date=February 1, 2012|access-date=February 20, 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120203225320/http://thecreatorsproject.com/blog/siren-seduction-qa-with-electronic-musician-grimes|archive-date=February 3, 2012|url-status=dead}}</ref>

===2011–2014: ''Visions''===
{{Main|Visions (Grimes album)|l1=''Visions''}}

Following extensive touring and positive reception to her first two albums and ''Darkbloom'' contribution, Grimes signed with record label 4AD in January 2012.<ref name="Sanneh">{{cite magazine|first=Kelefa|last=Sanneh|url=https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2015/09/28/pop-for-misfits|title=Pop for Misfits|magazine=[[The New Yorker]]|date=September 21, 2015|access-date=July 20, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160812075817/http://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2015/09/28/pop-for-misfits|archive-date=August 12, 2016|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Carrie Battan">{{cite web|first=Carrie|last=Battan|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/44967-grimes-signs-to-4ad-listen-to-new-track-genesis-from-visions|title=Grimes Signs to 4AD, Listen to New Track "Genesis" From Visions|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=January 4, 2012|access-date=January 13, 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120828101710/http://pitchfork.com/news/44967-grimes-signs-to-4ad-listen-to-new-track-genesis-from-visions|archive-date=August 28, 2012|url-status=live}}</ref> Her third studio album, ''[[Visions (Grimes album)|Visions]]'', was released on January 31, 2012, in Canada through Arbutus Records,<ref name="stereogum release date">{{cite web|first=Corban|last=Goble|url=https://www.stereogum.com/915242/grimes-genesis/news|title=Grimes – "Genesis"|work=[[Stereogum]]|date=January 4, 2012|access-date=August 4, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201201155829/https://www.stereogum.com/915242/grimes-genesis/news|archive-date=December 1, 2020|url-status=live}}</ref> February 21, 2012 in the United States through 4AD,<ref name="Carrie Battan"/><ref name="stereogum release date"/> and various dates in March 2012 elsewhere.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.jbhifionline.com.au/music/alternative/visions/662703|title=Visions – Grimes|work=[[JB Hi-Fi]]|access-date=June 10, 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140203001556/http://www.jbhifionline.com.au/music/alternative/visions/662703|archive-date=February 3, 2014|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.hmv.co.jp/en/artist_Grimes_000000000445463/item_Visions_5000945|title=Visions|work=[[HMV Japan]]|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230407070230/http://www.hmv.co.jp/en/artist_Grimes_000000000445463/item_Visions_5000945|archive-date=April 7, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> appeared on a number of publications' year-end lists and was considered Grimes' breakout album.<ref name="webby"/> ''[[NME]]'' included it on their [[NME's The 500 Greatest Albums of All Time|500 Greatest Albums of All Time]] list in 2013.<ref>{{cite web|first=Emily|last=Barker|url=https://www.nme.com/photos/the-500-greatest-albums-of-all-time-300-201-1426482|title=The 500 Greatest Albums Of All Time: 300-201|work=[[NME]]|date=October 24, 2013|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161202001900/https://www.nme.com/photos/the-500-greatest-albums-of-all-time-300-201-1426482|archive-date=December 2, 2016|url-status=live}}</ref> ''Visions'' won the Electronic Album of the Year Award and Grimes was nominated for the Breakthrough Artist of the Year at the [[Juno Award|Junos]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://junoawards.ca/nominees-winners/|title=2014 Nominees & Winners – The JUNO Awards|work=Juno Awards|access-date=August 4, 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130221085934/http://junoawards.ca/nominees-winners/|archive-date=February 21, 2013|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Gregory|last=Adams|url=https://exclaim.ca/music/article/leonard_cohen_weeknd_grimes_metric_classified_win_at_non-televised_juno_gala|title=Leonard Cohen, the Weeknd, Grimes, Metric, Classified Win Big at Non-Televised Juno Gala|work=[[Exclaim!]]|date=April 21, 2013|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022854/https://exclaim.ca/music/article/leonard_cohen_weeknd_grimes_metric_classified_win_at_non-televised_juno_gala|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> Grimes also won the Artist of the Year Award at the 2013 [[The Webby Awards|Webbys]].<ref name="webby">{{cite web|url=http://webbyawards.com/winners/2013/special-achievement/special-achievement/artist-of-the-year/grimes|title=Grimes|work=[[The Webby Awards]]|access-date=February 14, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170215121426/http://webbyawards.com/winners/2013/special-achievement/special-achievement/artist-of-the-year/grimes|archive-date=February 15, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|first=Adam|last=Carlson|url=https://ew.com/article/2013/04/30/frank-ocean-2013-webby-winners|title=Frank Ocean, The Onion, 'Burning Love' among 2013 Webby winners|magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]|date=April 30, 2013|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004132514/https://ew.com/article/2013/04/30/frank-ocean-2013-webby-winners/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>

{{Quote box|quote=[After nine days] you have no stimulation, so your subconscious starts filling in the blanks ... I started to feel like I was channelling spirits. I was convinced my music was a gift from God. It was like I knew exactly what to do next, as if my songs were already written. |source=Grimes in ''The Guardian'', April 27, 2012<ref name="nine" /> |width=30em |quoted=1}} The album's second single, "[[Oblivion (Grimes song)|Oblivion]]", was named the best song of 2012 by ''[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]''<ref>{{cite web|url=https://pitchfork.com/features/lists-and-guides/the-200-best-songs-of-the-2010s|title=The 200 Best Songs of the 2010s|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=October 7, 2019|access-date=October 20, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191011032035/https://pitchfork.com/features/lists-and-guides/the-200-best-songs-of-the-2010s|archive-date=October 11, 2019|url-status=live}}</ref> and was produced into a music video co-directed by [[Emily Kai Bock]] and Grimes.<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Ruth|last=Saxelby|url=https://www.dummymag.com/features/the-story-behind-grimes-s-oblivion-video|title=The story behind Grimes's 'Oblivion' video|magazine=Dummymag|date=June 3, 2012|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004135349/https://dmy.co/features/the-story-behind-grimes-s-oblivion-video|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Ryan|last=Dombal|url=https://pitchfork.com/features/directors-cut/8783-grimes-oblivion|title=Grimes: "Oblivion"|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=March 5, 2012|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406155355/https://pitchfork.com/features/directors-cut/8783-grimes-oblivion/|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> ''[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]'' ranked "Oblivion" at number one on their 200 Best Tracks of the Decade So Far list in 2014.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://pitchfork.com/features/staff-lists/9466-the-top-200-tracks-of-2010-2014/10|title=The 200 Best Tracks of the Decade So Far (2010–2014) – Pitchfork|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|access-date=May 28, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150601044837/http://pitchfork.com/features/staff-lists/9466-the-top-200-tracks-of-2010-2014/10|archive-date=June 1, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref> In interviews following the album's release, Grimes explained that she was assigned a strict deadline by which to have her third album finished far before it was complete,<ref>{{cite web|first=Jeff|last=Benjamin|url=http://www.fuse.tv/videos/2015/12/grimes-fuse-first-art-angels-visions-interview|title=Grimes: 'Visions' Has "Filler" Material Compared to 'Art Angels'|work=[[Fuse (TV channel)|Fuse]]|date=December 9, 2015|access-date=July 24, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161021000646/http://www.fuse.tv/videos/2015/12/grimes-fuse-first-art-angels-visions-interview|archive-date=October 21, 2016|url-status=live}}</ref> resulting in her recording the bulk of ''Visions'' while isolated in her Montreal apartment in [[Mile End, Montreal|Mile End]]<ref>{{cite web|first=Alyssa|last=Noel|url=https://www.spin.com/2012/06/burning-down-loft-inside-montreals-diy-scene/|title=Burning Down the Loft: Inside Montreal's DIY Scene|magazine=[[Spin (magazine)|Spin]]|date=June 12, 2012|access-date=August 20, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230402085957/https://www.spin.com/2012/06/burning-down-loft-inside-montreals-diy-scene/|archive-date=April 2, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> for three consecutive weeks. Notably, this intensive recording session included a period of nine days without sleep or food and with [[Blackout (fabric)|blacked out]] windows, since she generally could not make music as readily during the day, and doing "tons of [[amphetamines]]"<ref name="nine">{{cite web|first=Sam|last=Richards|url=https://www.theguardian.com/music/2012/apr/28/grimes-visions-montreal|title=Grimes: nine days without food, sleep or company gave me ''Visions''|work=[[The Guardian]]|date=April 27, 2012|access-date=June 15, 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131112220119/http://www.theguardian.com/music/2012/apr/28/grimes-visions-montreal|archive-date=November 12, 2013|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Altered Zone">{{cite web|first=Lisa|last=Hresko|url=http://www.cmj.com/feature/in-an-altered-zone|title=In An Altered Zone|work=[[CMJ]]|date=March 3, 2012|access-date=August 1, 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131019120433/http://www.cmj.com/feature/in-an-altered-zone|archive-date=October 19, 2013|url-status=dead}}</ref> She described the writing process as being "equally enjoyable and tortuous",<ref name=7dig/> feeling that its difficulty contributed to its success.<ref name=7dig>{{cite web|url=http://www.7digital.com/features/interviews/grimes|title=7Digital Interview 2012|work=[[7digital]]|access-date=June 26, 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141208181713/http://www.7digital.com/features/interviews/grimes|archive-date=December 8, 2014|url-status=dead}}</ref> Grimes went on the Visions Tour from 2012 to 2014 with supporting acts [[Born Gold]], Myths, [[Elite Gymnastics]], and Ami Dang.<ref name="Visions Tour Born Gold">{{cite web|first=Ben|last=Kaye|url=https://consequence.net/2011/11/grimes-schedules-spring-2012-tour-dates|title=Grimes schedules Spring 2012 tour dates|work=[[Consequence (publication)|Consequence]]|date=November 22, 2011|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004154223/https://consequence.net/2011/11/grimes-schedules-spring-2012-tour-dates/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Visions Tour Myths and Elite Gymnastics">{{cite web|first= E.|last=Nagurney|url=https://www.tinymixtapes.com/news/grimes-announces-mythical-gymnastics-tour-with-myths-and-elite-gymnastics|title=Grimes schedules Spring 2012 tour dates|work=[[Tiny Mix Tapes]]|date=June 11, 2012|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406031402/https://www.tinymixtapes.com/news/grimes-announces-mythical-gymnastics-tour-with-myths-and-elite-gymnastics|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Visions Tour factmag">{{cite magazine|url=https://www.factmag.com/2012/12/03/grimes-announces-world-tour-dates|title=Grimes announces world tour dates|magazine=[[Fact (UK magazine)|Factmag]]|date=December 3, 2012|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004132616/https://www.factmag.com/2012/12/03/grimes-announces-world-tour-dates/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> From March 23–25, Grimes staged an art show and charity auction at the Audio Visual Arts (AVA) gallery in New York City, featuring paintings and drawings.<ref>{{cite web|first=Jenn|last=Pelly|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/45692-grimes-claire-boucher-to-stage-art-show-in-nyc/|title=Grimes' Claire Boucher to Stage Art Show in NYC|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=March 8, 2012|access-date=April 5, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170309065138/http://pitchfork.com/news/45692-grimes-claire-boucher-to-stage-art-show-in-nyc/|archive-date=March 9, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref> In March 2012, Grimes collaborated with Cop Car Bonfire's Tim Lafontaine and went under the name, Membrain.<ref name="Membrain pitchfork">{{cite web|first=Carrie|last=Battan|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/45912-listen-to-grimes-side-project-membrain|title=Listen to Grimes Side Project Membrain|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=March 26, 2012|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004131939/https://pitchfork.com/news/45912-listen-to-grimes-side-project-membrain/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Membrain factmag">{{cite magazine|url=https://www.factmag.com/2012/03/26/membrain-a-new-project-from-grimes-and-cop-car-bonfire|title=Stream two tracks by Membrain, a new project from Grimes|magazine=[[Fact (UK magazine)|Factmag]]|date=March 26, 2012|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004132634/https://www.factmag.com/2012/03/26/membrain-a-new-project-from-grimes-and-cop-car-bonfire/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> They released an EP called, ''Sit Back, Rewind''.<ref name="Membrain pitchfork"/><ref name="Membrain factmag"/> In May 2012, Grimes was featured on [[BloodPop|Blood Diamonds]]'s song "Phone Sex".<ref>{{cite web|first=Evan|last=Minsker|url=https://pitchfork.com/reviews/tracks/13675-blood-diamonds-phone-sex-ft-grimes|title=BloodPop®: "Phone Sex" ft. Grimes Track Review|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=May 30, 2012|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004133018/https://pitchfork.com/reviews/tracks/13675-blood-diamonds-phone-sex-ft-grimes/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Gregory|last=Adams|url=https://exclaim.ca/music/article/blood_diamonds_details_phone_sex_12-inch_with_grimes|title=Blood Diamonds Details 'Phone Sex' 12-Inch with Grimes|work=[[Exclaim!]]|date=May 30, 2012|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022854/https://exclaim.ca/music/article/blood_diamonds_details_phone_sex_12-inch_with_grimes|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> In July 2012, Grimes toured as a supporting act with [[Diplo]] and [[Skrillex]] on the Full Flex Express Canadian Train Tour.<ref name="Full Flex Express Canadian Train Tour">{{cite web|first=Gregory|last=Adams|url=https://exclaim.ca/music/article/full_flex_express_tour_to_travel_across_canada_with_skrillex_grimes_diplo|title="Full Flex Express Tour" to Travel Across Canada with Skrillex, Grimes, Diplo|work=[[Exclaim!]]|date=May 8, 2012|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022856/https://exclaim.ca/music/article/full_flex_express_tour_to_travel_across_canada_with_skrillex_grimes_diplo|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Full Flex Express Canadian Train Tour2">{{cite web|first=Michael|last=Roffman|url=https://consequence.net/2012/05/skrillex-diplo-and-grimes-announce-full-flex-express-tour|title=Skrillex, Diplo, and Grimes announce Full Flex Express Tour|work=[[Consequence (publication)|Consequence]]|date=May 8, 2012|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230531095459/https://consequence.net/2012/05/skrillex-diplo-and-grimes-announce-full-flex-express-tour/|archive-date=May 31, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> In August 2012, Grimes made her American television debut on ''[[Late Night With Jimmy Fallon]]''.<ref>{{cite web|first=Carrie|last=Battan|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/47421-grimes-to-make-us-tv-debut-on-fallon|title=Grimes to Make U.S. TV Debut on "Fallon"|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=August 7, 2012|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004135322/https://pitchfork.com/news/47421-grimes-to-make-us-tv-debut-on-fallon/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Michael|last=Roffman|url=https://consequence.net/2012/08/video-grimes-on-jimmy-fallon|title=Video: Grimes on Jimmy Fallon|work=[[Consequence (publication)|Consequence]]|date=August 15, 2012|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004134005/https://consequence.net/2012/08/video-grimes-on-jimmy-fallon/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>

In April 2013, Grimes posted a written statement addressing her experience as a female musician as rife with sexism and expressed disappointment that her feminist stance was often interpreted as anti-male.<ref>{{cite web|first=Jason|last=Newman|url=https://www.fuse.tv/2013/04/grimes-sexism-post|title=Grimes Lashes Out at Sexists: "I Don't Want to Be Molested at Shows"|work=[[Fuse (TV channel)|Fuse]]|date=April 24, 2013|access-date=July 24, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201020234358/https://www.fuse.tv/2013/04/grimes-sexism-post|archive-date=October 20, 2020|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|first=RJ|last=Cubarrubia|url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/news/grimes-rails-against-sexism-im-done-with-being-passive-20130424|title=Grimes Rails Against Sexism: 'I'm Done With Being Passive'|magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]|date=April 24, 2013|access-date=June 16, 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130715011654/http://www.rollingstone.com/music/news/grimes-rails-against-sexism-im-done-with-being-passive-20130424|archive-date=July 15, 2013|url-status=live}}</ref> When speaking about her preference to produce all her studio albums herself, she said, "I don't wanna be just like the face of this thing I built, I want to be the one who built it".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fi2N5KHgO80|title=Grimes – Art Angel (Documentary)|work=[[The Fader]]|via=[[YouTube]]|date=December 10, 2015|access-date=October 31, 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160804234628/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fi2N5KHgO80|archive-date=August 4, 2016|url-status=live}}</ref> In December 2013, Grimes employed the services of [[Jay-Z]]'s management company, [[Roc Nation]].<ref>{{cite web|first=Alex|last=Young|url=https://consequence.net/2013/12/grimes-signs-to-jay-zs-roc-nation|title=Grimes signs to Jay Z's Roc Nation|work=[[Consequence (publication)|Consequence]]|date=December 17, 2013|access-date=December 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004132308/https://consequence.net/2013/12/grimes-signs-to-jay-zs-roc-nation/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Chris|last=Martins|url=https://www.spin.com/2013/12/grimes-roc-nation-signed-jay-z-claire-boucher|title=Grimes Signs to Jay Z's Roc Nation|work=[[Spin (magazine)|Spin]]|date=December 17, 2013|access-date=July 23, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150725073912/http://www.spin.com/2013/12/grimes-roc-nation-signed-jay-z-claire-boucher|archive-date=July 25, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref>

===2014–2017: ''Art Angels''===
{{Main|Art Angels|l1=''Art Angels''}}
[[File:Grimes Governors Ball 2014 05.png|thumb|Grimes performing at the [[Governors Ball]] in June 2014]]

On June 26, 2014, Grimes premiered the new track "Go", produced by and featuring [[Blood Diamonds (music producer)|Blood Diamonds]]. It was a track that had been written for and rejected by [[Rihanna]] and was premiered on Zane Lowe's radio 1 show.<ref>{{cite web|first=Emily|last=Blake|url=http://www.mtv.com/news/1855973/grimes-go-rihanna-rejected|title=Hear 'Go,' The Grimes Song That Rihanna Rejected|work=[[MTV News]]|date=June 26, 2014|access-date=April 13, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170413235113/http://www.mtv.com/news/1855973/grimes-go-rihanna-rejected|archive-date=April 13, 2017|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Lauren|last=Nostro|url=http://www.complex.com/music/2014/06/grimes-go-f-blood-diamonds|title=Listen to Grimes' "Go" f/ Blood Diamonds|work=Complex|date=June 26, 2014|access-date=August 4, 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140802053314/http://www.complex.com/music/2014/06/grimes-go-f-blood-diamonds|archive-date=August 2, 2014|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Amy|last=Phillips|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/56329-grimes-previews-sweeping-go-video|title=Grimes Previews Sweeping "Go" Video|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=August 21, 2014|access-date=August 22, 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140821224612/http://pitchfork.com/news/56329-grimes-previews-sweeping-go-video|archive-date=August 21, 2014|url-status=live}}</ref> ''[[Rolling Stone]]'' ranked it number fourteen on their Best Songs of 2014 list.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/lists/50-best-songs-of-2014-20141203/grimes-go-20141202|title=Grimes, "Go"|magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]|date=December 3, 2014|access-date=December 12, 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141225014901/http://www.rollingstone.com/music/lists/50-best-songs-of-2014-20141203/grimes-go-20141202|archive-date=December 25, 2014|url-status=live}}</ref> In July 2014, Grimes was featured on [[Bleachers (band)|Bleachers]]' song "Take Me Away" from their album, ''[[Strange Desire]]''.<ref>{{cite web|first=Jeremy|last=Gordon|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/55887-grimes-teams-with-bleachers-for-take-me-away|title=Grimes Teams With Bleachers for "Take Me Away"|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=July 14, 2014|access-date=December 11, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230710030816/https://pitchfork.com/news/55887-grimes-teams-with-bleachers-for-take-me-away/|archive-date=July 10, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> On August 19, 2014, Grimes was featured in the music for the remix of [[Haim (band)|Haim]]'s ''[[My Song 5]]''.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.pastemagazine.com/music/haim/watch-haims-daytime-tv-inspired-my-song-5-video|title=Watch Haim's Daytime TV-Inspired "My Song 5" Video|magazine=[[Paste (magazine)|Paste]]|date=August 19, 2014|access-date=December 11, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230709184602/https://www.pastemagazine.com/music/haim/watch-haims-daytime-tv-inspired-my-song-5-video|archive-date=July 9, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|first=Colin|last=Stutz|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/haim-release-full-my-song-5-music-video-with-vanessa-bayer-kesha-aap-ferg-6221828|title=Haim Release Full 'My Song 5' Music Video With Vanessa Bayer, Kesha, A$AP Ferg, Grimes & More|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|date=August 19, 2014|access-date=December 11, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004132339/https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/haim-release-full-my-song-5-music-video-with-vanessa-bayer-kesha-aap-ferg-6221828/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>

On March 8, 2015, Grimes released a self-directed video for a demo version of "[[Realiti (song)|Realiti]]" from an abandoned album. It received critical acclaim from music critics, being named Best New Music by Jenn Pelly from ''Pitchfork'', calling it the "best new Grimes song since ''Visions''".<ref>{{cite web|first=Zoe|last=Camp|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/58769-grimes-shares-video-for-previously-unheard-track-realiti|title=Grimes Shares Video for Previously-Unheard Track "REALiTi"|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=March 9, 2015|access-date=May 8, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150504125810/http://pitchfork.com/news/58769-grimes-shares-video-for-previously-unheard-track-realiti|archive-date=May 4, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Jenn|last=Pelly|url=https://pitchfork.com/reviews/tracks/17367-grimes-realiti|title=Grimes|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|access-date=July 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150529180138/http://pitchfork.com/reviews/tracks/17367-grimes-realiti|archive-date=May 29, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref> On March 15, 2015, Grimes and [[Bleachers (band)|Bleachers]] released their collaboration, "Entropy" for the HBO TV show ''[[Girls (TV series)|Girls]]''.<ref>{{cite web|first=Tom|last=Breihan|url=https://www.stereogum.com/1787667/grimes-bleachers-entropy/news|title=Grimes & Bleachers – "Entropy"|work=[[Stereogum]]|date=March 15, 2015|access-date=December 11, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004135934/https://www.stereogum.com/1787667/grimes-bleachers-entropy/news/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Zoe|last=Camp|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/58252-grimes-and-bleachers-share-entropy-from-hbos-girls|title=Grimes and Bleachers Share "Entropy" From HBO's "Girls"|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=March 15, 2015|access-date=July 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150512170821/http://pitchfork.com/news/58252-grimes-and-bleachers-share-entropy-from-hbos-girls|archive-date=May 12, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref> In the summer of 2015, Grimes toured with [[Lana Del Rey]] for several of her [[The Endless Summer Tour|Endless Summer Tour]] dates.<ref name="Endless Summer Tour">{{cite web|first=Alex|last=Young|url=https://consequence.net/2015/04/lana-del-rey-and-grimes-team-up-for-the-endless-summer-tour|title=Lana Del Rey and Grimes team up for The Endless Summer Tour|work=[[Consequence (publication)|Consequence]]|date=April 1, 2015|access-date=December 11, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220720063921/https://consequence.net/2015/04/lana-del-rey-and-grimes-team-up-for-the-endless-summer-tour/|archive-date=July 20, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Endless Summer Tour2">{{cite magazine|first=Ryan|last=Reed|url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/lana-del-rey-recruits-grimes-for-endless-summer-tour-79491|title=Lana Del Rey Recruits Grimes for 'Endless Summer' Tour|magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]|date=April 1, 2015|access-date=July 25, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220310075926/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/lana-del-rey-recruits-grimes-for-endless-summer-tour-79491|archive-date=March 10, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref> She then toured in the fall of 2015 as the headliner of her own Rhinestone Cowgirls Tour with opener [[Nicole Dollanganger]].<ref name="Rhinestone Cowgirls Tour">{{cite web|first= Michael|last=Roffman|url=https://consequence.net/2015/09/grimes-announces-rhinestone-cowgirls-fall-tour-dates|title=Grimes announces Rhinestone Cowgirls fall tour dates|work=[[Consequence (publication)|Consequence]]|date=September 14, 2015|access-date=July 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160429193216/http://consequenceofsound.net/2015/09/grimes-announces-rhinestone-cowgirls-fall-tour-dates|archive-date=April 29, 2016|url-status=live}}</ref>

Speaking of her upcoming fourth album, scheduled for a "surprise" release in October, Grimes said that record was recorded with "real instruments", a departure from the primarily synth and sampler driven composing of her prior releases.<ref name="new album">{{cite web|first=Evan|last=Minsker|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/59687-grimes-says-new-album-coming-in-october|title=Grimes Says New Album Coming in October|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=May 24, 2015|access-date=August 29, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150829082422/http://pitchfork.com/news/59687-grimes-says-new-album-coming-in-october|archive-date=August 29, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref> On October 26, 2015, Grimes released the lead single of the album, "[[Flesh Without Blood]]", as well as a two-act music video comprising both "Flesh Without Blood" and "Life in the Vivid Dream", another song from the upcoming album.<ref name="Flesh Without Blood/Life in the Vivid Dream">{{cite web|first=Matthew|last=Strauss|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/61760-grimes-releases-flesh-without-bloodlife-in-the-vivid-dream-video-announces-art-angels-details|title=Grimes Releases "Flesh Without Blood/Life in the Vivid Dream" Video, Announces Art Angels Details|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=October 26, 2015|access-date=December 11, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230401195750/https://pitchfork.com/news/61760-grimes-releases-flesh-without-bloodlife-in-the-vivid-dream-video-announces-art-angels-details/|archive-date=April 1, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Hazel|last=Cills|url=https://pitchfork.com/reviews/tracks/17777-grimes-flesh-without-blood|title=Grimes "Flesh without Blood"|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=October 26, 2015|access-date=October 27, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151027131036/http://pitchfork.com/reviews/tracks/17777-grimes-flesh-without-blood|archive-date=October 27, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref> The album, titled ''[[Art Angels]]'', was released in November to favourable reviews, garnering an 88 (out of 100) rating on [[Metacritic]]<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.metacritic.com/music/art-angels/grimes|title=Art Angels by Grimes|website=Metacritic|access-date=November 10, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151108234900/http://www.metacritic.com/music/art-angels/grimes|archive-date=November 8, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref> and the Best New Music designation from ''Pitchfork''. Jessica Hopper of ''Pitchfork'' described ''Art Angels'' as "evidence of Boucher's labor and an articulation of a pop vision that is incontrovertibly hers... an epic holiday buffet of tendentious feminist fuck-off, with second helpings for anonymous commenters and music industry blood-suckers".<ref>{{cite web|first=Jessica|last=Hopper|url=https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/21264-art-angels|title=Art Angels Grimes|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=November 10, 2015|access-date=July 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160515192341/http://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/21264-art-angels|archive-date=May 15, 2016|url-status=live}}</ref>

''Art Angels'' was named best album of the year by ''[[NME]]'', ''[[Exclaim!]]'', and ''[[Stereogum]]''.<ref>{{cite web|first=David|last=Renshaw|url=https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-21-1205841|title=Grimes reacts to 'Art Angels' being named NME's album of the year 2015: 'It's dreamlike'|work=[[NME]]|date=December 2, 2015|access-date=February 23, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170224052646/http://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-21-1205841|archive-date=February 24, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://exclaim.ca/music/article/exclaims_top_20_pop_rock_albums_part_two-best_of_2015/page/11|title=Exclaim!'s Top 20 Pop & Rock Albums, Part Two|work=[[Exclaim!]]|date=December 3, 2015|access-date=July 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151208121904/http://exclaim.ca/music/article/exclaims_top_20_pop_rock_albums_part_two-best_of_2015/page/11|archive-date=December 8, 2015|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.stereogum.com/1845609/the-50-best-albums-of-2015/franchises/2015-in-review/5|title=The 50 Best Albums Of 2015|work=[[Stereogum]]|date=December 1, 2015|access-date=July 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151209031602/http://www.stereogum.com/1845609/the-50-best-albums-of-2015/franchises/2015-in-review/5|archive-date=December 9, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref> It peaked at number 1 on the ''[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]'' US Top Alternative Album Chart<ref>{{Cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/artist/grimes/chart-history/alt|title=Grimes Chart History Top Alternative Albums|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|access-date=July 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200303060320/https://www.billboard.com/music/Grimes/chart-history/ALT|archive-date=March 3, 2020|url-status=live}}</ref> and number 2 on the ''Billboard'' Top Independent Album chart.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/artist/grimes/chart-history/ind|title=Grimes – Chart History: Independent Albums|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|access-date=July 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200303060332/https://www.billboard.com/music/Grimes/chart-history/IND|archive-date=March 3, 2020|url-status=live}}</ref> Grimes won the 2016 International award at the Socan Annual Awards and the 2016 Harper's Bazaar Musician of the Year Award in October.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.socan.ca/news/socan-montr%C3%A9al-awards-2016-celebrate-music-creators-publishers|title=SOCAN Montréal Awards 2016 to celebrate music creators, publishers|website=Socan.ca|access-date=February 23, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170224054049/https://www.socan.ca/news/socan-montr%C3%A9al-awards-2016-celebrate-music-creators-publishers|archive-date=February 24, 2017|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Peter|last=Helman|url=https://www.stereogum.com/1908732/grimes-wins-harpers-bazaar-women-of-the-year-award/news|title=Grimes Wins Harper's Bazaar Women Of The Year Award|work=[[Stereogum]]|date=October 31, 2016|access-date=February 23, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170224131551/http://www.stereogum.com/1908732/grimes-wins-harpers-bazaar-women-of-the-year-award/news|archive-date=February 24, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref>

[[File:Grimes, Lollapalooza 2016, Chicago (29078521595).jpg|thumb|left|Grimes performing at [[Lollapalooza]] 2016]]

In the spring of 2016, Grimes toured Asia and Europe with supporting act [[Hana Pestle|Hana]] on the Ac!d Reign Tour.<ref name="Hana Ac!d Reign Tour">{{cite web|first=Jazz|last=Monroe|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/61489-grimes-announces-acd-reign-european-tour|title=Grimes Announces "Ac!d Reign" European Tour – Pitchfork|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=October 5, 2015|access-date=July 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160524134538/http://pitchfork.com/news/61489-grimes-announces-acd-reign-european-tour|archive-date=May 24, 2016|url-status=live}}</ref> Grimes continued touring through the summer of 2016, performing at various music festivals across North America and opening for [[Florence and the Machine]] on select dates of the [[How Big, How Blue, How Beautiful Tour|How Beautiful Tour]].<ref name="Grimes Florence and the Machine">{{cite web|first=Amy|last=Phillips|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/59226-grimes-to-open-for-florence-and-the-machine-on-north-american-tour|title=Grimes to Open for Florence and the Machine on North American Tour|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=January 11, 2016|access-date=July 20, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160503100534/http://pitchfork.com/news/59226-grimes-to-open-for-florence-and-the-machine-on-north-american-tour|archive-date=May 3, 2016|url-status=live}}</ref>

Continuing the series of music videos for songs off ''Art Angels'' that began with "Flesh Without Blood" and "Life in the Vivid Dream" ("Act I" and "Act II", respectively),<ref name="Flesh Without Blood/Life in the Vivid Dream"/> Grimes released the music video for "Kill V. Maim" ("Act III") on January 19, 2016,<ref>{{cite web|first=Ben|last=Kaye|url=https://consequence.net/2016/01/grimes-and-her-art-angels-rule-the-world-in-video-for-kill-v-maim-watch|title=Grimes and her Art Angels rule the world in video for "Kill V. Maim" — watch|work=[[Consequence (publication)|Consequence]]|date=January 19, 2016|access-date=December 11, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004134007/https://consequence.net/2016/01/grimes-and-her-art-angels-rule-the-world-in-video-for-kill-v-maim-watch/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> and the music video for "California" ("Act IV") on May 9, 2016.<ref>{{cite web|first=Eddie|last=Fu|url=https://uproxx.com/music/grimes-california-new-music-video|title=Grimes Dances Up A Storm In Her New Music Video For 'California'|work=[[Uproxx]]|date=May 9, 2016|access-date=December 11, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004132610/https://uproxx.com/music/grimes-california-new-music-video/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> Grimes crafted a slightly remixed version of "California" for the music video to achieve a less "dissonant" visual/auditory mix.<ref>{{cite web|first=Dee|last=Lockett|url=https://www.vulture.com/2016/05/watch-grimess-remixed-california-video.html|title=Drown Yourself in the Surreal Technicolor World of Grimes's 'California' Video|work=[[Vulture (website)|Vulture]]|date=May 9, 2016|access-date=July 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170425144629/http://www.vulture.com/2016/05/watch-grimess-remixed-california-video.html|archive-date=April 25, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref> On August 3, 2016, Grimes released the song "Medieval Warfare" as part of the [[Suicide Squad (soundtrack)|soundtrack]] of the 2016 superhero film, ''[[Suicide Squad (2016 film)|Suicide Squad]]''.<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Ryan|last=Reed|url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/news/hear-grimes-dark-suicide-squad-song-medieval-warfare-w432538|title=Hear Grimes' Dark 'Suicide Squad' Song 'Medieval Warfare' – Rolling Stone|magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]|date=August 3, 2016|access-date=July 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170911211458/http://www.rollingstone.com/music/news/hear-grimes-dark-suicide-squad-song-medieval-warfare-w432538|archive-date=September 11, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Sheldon|last=Pearce|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/66200-listen-to-grimes-new-song-medieval-warfare-from-suicide-squad/|title=Listen to Grimes' New Song "Medieval Warfare" From Suicide Squad|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=August 3, 2016|access-date=December 11, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230125122524/https://pitchfork.com/news/66200-listen-to-grimes-new-song-medieval-warfare-from-suicide-squad/|archive-date=January 25, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>

On October 5, 2016, Grimes with friend and collaborator Hana Pestle, more commonly known by stage name [[Hana Pestle|Hana]], released "The Ac!d Reign Chronicles", a lo-fi series of seven music videos including songs by Grimes ("Butterfly", "World Princess Part II", "Belly of the Beat" and "Scream") and Hana ("Underwater", "Chimera" and "Avalanche"), each starring in their respective segments.<ref name="NME Ac!d Reign Chronicles">{{cite web|first=Larry|last=Bartleet|url=https://www.nme.com/blogs/nme-blogs/grimes-and-hana-s-seven-videos-are-yet-more-evidence-of-their-awesome-friendship-1188418|title=Grimes And Hana's Seven Videos Are Our New Friendship Goals|work=[[NME]]|date=October 6, 2016|access-date=December 11, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022858/https://www.nme.com/blogs/nme-blogs/grimes-and-hana-s-seven-videos-are-yet-more-evidence-of-their-awesome-friendship-1188418|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="MTV Ac!d Reign Chronicles">{{cite web|first=Madeline|last=Roth|url=https://www.mtv.com/news/o4n8q5/grimes-acid-reigns-chronicle-video-series|title=Grimes Drops Seven Whimsical Music Videos Shot Only On Cell Phones|work=[[MTV News]]|date=October 5, 2016|access-date=December 11, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406024357/https://www.mtv.com/news/o4n8q5/grimes-acid-reigns-chronicle-video-series|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref name="rollingstone Ac!d Reign Chronicles">{{cite magazine|first1=Ryan|last1=Reed|first2=Sarah|last2=Grant|url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/news/watch-grimes-quirky-acd-reign-chronicles-video-series-w443586|title=Watch Grimes' Quirky 'Ac!d Reign Chronicles' Video Series|magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]|date=October 5, 2016|access-date=July 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170827235129/http://www.rollingstone.com/music/news/watch-grimes-quirky-acd-reign-chronicles-video-series-w443586|archive-date=August 27, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref> Additional appearances include Aristophanes in Scream<ref name="MTV Ac!d Reign Chronicles"/><ref name="rollingstone Ac!d Reign Chronicles"/> and two of Grimes' backup dancers, Linda Davis and Alyson Van, throughout the series.<ref name="NME Ac!d Reign Chronicles"/> "The AC!D Reign Chronicles" were recorded over the course of two weeks during the duo's time touring Europe and were made with minimal production,<ref name="NME Ac!d Reign Chronicles"/> shot exclusively on iPhones with no crew aside from her brother, Mac Boucher, who assisted with filming.<ref name="rollingstone Ac!d Reign Chronicles"/> In 2016, Grimes co-wrote the song "[[Heaven (Troye Sivan song)|Heaven]]" for [[Troye Sivan]]'s album ''[[Blue Neighbourhood]]''.<ref>{{cite web|first=Melanie|last=Gomez|url=https://celebmix.com/troye-sivan-releases-one-of-his-most-personal-songs-as-his-new-single-heaven|title=Troye Sivan Releases One Of His Most Personal Songs As His New Single, "Heaven"|work=CelebMix|date=October 19, 2016|access-date=December 11, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230709181100/https://celebmix.com/troye-sivan-releases-one-of-his-most-personal-songs-as-his-new-single-heaven/|archive-date=July 9, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>

On February 2, 2017, Grimes premiered on [[Tidal (service)|Tidal]] the high budget futuristic music video of "Venus Fly", starring herself and [[Janelle Monáe]].<ref>{{cite web|first=Amy|last=Phillips|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/71296-watch-grimes-and-janelle-monaes-futuristic-cybergoth-venus-fly-video/|title=Watch Grimes and Janelle Monáe's Futuristic Cybergoth "Venus Fly" Video|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=February 2, 2017|access-date=December 11, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230330124507/https://pitchfork.com/news/71296-watch-grimes-and-janelle-monaes-futuristic-cybergoth-venus-fly-video/|archive-date=March 30, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=James|last=Rettig|url=https://www.stereogum.com/1922706/grimes-venus-fly-feat-janelle-monae-video/video|title=Grimes – "Venus Fly" (Feat. Janelle Monáe) Video|work=[[Stereogum]]|date=February 2, 2017|access-date=July 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170218063424/http://www.stereogum.com/1922706/grimes-venus-fly-feat-janelle-monae-video/video|archive-date=February 18, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref> The video was uploaded on YouTube on February 9, 2017.<ref>{{cite magazine|first=E.C.|last=Flamming|url=https://www.pastemagazine.com/music/grimes-/watch-grimes-video-venus-fly-featuring-janelle-mon|title=Watch Grimes' "Venus Fly" Video Featuring Janelle Monae|magazine=[[Paste (magazine)|Paste]]|date=February 9, 2017|access-date=July 21, 2022|archive-date=July 22, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220722035549/https://www.pastemagazine.com/music/grimes-/watch-grimes-video-venus-fly-featuring-janelle-mon/|url-status=dead}}</ref> She won Best Dance Video for "Venus Fly" at the Much Music Video Awards.<ref>{{cite web|first=Mike|last=Vulpo|url=http://www.eonline.com/news/860853/iheartradio-much-music-video-awards-2017-winners-the-complete-list|title=iHeartRadio Much Music Video Awards 2017 Winners: The Complete List|work=[[E!|E! Online]]|date=June 18, 2017|access-date=July 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170908202027/http://www.eonline.com/news/860853/iheartradio-much-music-video-awards-2017-winners-the-complete-list|archive-date=September 8, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref> In 2017, Grimes won a JUNO Award for Video of the Year, featuring "Kill V. Maim".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://exclaim.ca/music/article/here_is_the_full_list_of_2017_juno_winners|title=Here Is the Full List of 2017 Juno Winners|work=[[Exclaim!]]|date=April 2, 2017|access-date=December 11, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230314213124/https://exclaim.ca/music/article/here_is_the_full_list_of_2017_juno_winners|archive-date=March 14, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> On October 19, 2017, Grimes released a cover of [[Tegan and Sara]]'s "Dark Come Soon" with [[Hana (American musician)|Hana]].<ref name="Dark Come Soon">{{cite web|first=Alex|last=Young|url=https://consequence.net/2017/10/grimes-covers-tegan-and-saras-dark-come-soon-stream|title=Grimes covers Tegan and Sara's "Dark Come Soon": Stream|work=[[Consequence (publication)|Consequence]]|date=October 20, 2017|access-date=December 11, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004133909/https://consequence.net/2017/10/grimes-covers-tegan-and-saras-dark-come-soon-stream/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Dark Come Soon2">{{cite web|first=Sam|last=Sodomsky|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-and-hana-cover-tegan-and-sara-listen/|title=Grimes and Hana Cover Tegan and Sara: Listen|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=October 19, 2017|access-date=December 11, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230609090802/https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-and-hana-cover-tegan-and-sara-listen/|archive-date=June 9, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> The cover is a part of Tegan and Sara's ''[[The Con (album)#Tegan and Sara Present the Con X: Covers|The Con X: Covers album]]''.<ref name="Dark Come Soon"/><ref name="Dark Come Soon2"/>
{{clear}}

===2018–2021: ''Miss Anthropocene'' and collaborations===
{{Main|Miss Anthropocene|l1=''Miss Anthropocene''}}

In February 2018, Grimes wrote on [[Instagram]], "welp no music any time soon after all".<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Jordan|last=Darville|url=http://www.thefader.com/2018/02/15/grimes-lp5-fifth-album-update-trash-industry|title=Grimes says "no music any time soon," blames "trash music industry"|magazine=[[The Fader]]|date=February 15, 2018|access-date=July 19, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180217024037/http://www.thefader.com/2018/02/15/grimes-lp5-fifth-album-update-trash-industry|archive-date=February 17, 2018|url-status=live}}</ref> It was later revealed that this was due to a clash with her label, 4AD.<ref>{{cite web|first=Nick|last=Reilly|url=https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-has-delivered-a-disappointing-update-on-her-next-album-2243472|title=Grimes has delivered a disappointing update on her next album|work=[[NME]]|date=February 16, 2018|access-date=February 16, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180216165028/http://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-has-delivered-a-disappointing-update-on-her-next-album-2243472|archive-date=February 16, 2018|url-status=live}}</ref> She later revealed on an Instagram post that she would eventually be releasing two albums, and that "they would be separated by a period of time", with the first being released with 4AD, and the second with an undisclosed label. Grimes stated that this first album would be "highly collaborative and [characterized by] most glorious light", with the second highlighting themes of "pure darkness and chaos".<ref name="final album for my label">{{cite web|url=https://consequence.net/2018/02/grimes-says-her-final-album-for-my-shit-label-will-be-highly-collaborative|title=Grimes says her "final album for my shit label" will be "highly collaborative"|work=[[Consequence (publication)|Consequence]]|date=February 26, 2018|access-date=March 6, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180307151025/https://consequenceofsound.net/2018/02/grimes-says-her-final-album-for-my-shit-label-will-be-highly-collaborative|archive-date=March 7, 2018|url-status=live}}</ref>

On April 10, 2018, Grimes was featured on "[[Pynk]]", the third single from [[Janelle Monáe]]'s album, ''[[Dirty Computer]]''.<ref>{{cite web|first=Gabriela|last=Tully Claymore|url=https://www.stereogum.com/1990705/janelle-monae-pynk-feat-grimes/music|title=Janelle Monáe – "Pynk" (Feat. Grimes) Video|work=[[Stereogum]]|date=April 10, 2018|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230709195937/https://www.stereogum.com/1990705/janelle-monae-pynk-feat-grimes/music/|archive-date=July 9, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Sam|last=Sodomsky|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-joins-janelle-monae-for-new-song-pynk-listen|title=Janelle Monáe and Grimes Share New Song and Video "Pynk": Watch|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=April 10, 2018|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230330171435/https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-joins-janelle-monae-for-new-song-pynk-listen/|archive-date=March 30, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> On May 30, 2018, Grimes was featured on "Love4Eva" by [[yyxy|Loona yyxy]], the lead single from South Korean girl group [[Loona]]'s third sub-unit's debut EP ''[[Beauty & the Beat (EP)|Beauty & the Beat]]''.<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Tamar|last=Herman|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/grimes-loona-unit-yyxy-love4eva-8457769|title=Grimes Teams Up With K-Pop Girl Group Loona for Unit yyxy's Upcoming 'Love4eva' Single|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|date=May 24, 2018|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004132400/https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/grimes-loona-unit-yyxy-love4eva-8457769/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Michelle Hyun|last=Kim|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-joins-k-pop-group-loona-on-new-song-love4eva-listen|title=Grimes Joins K-Pop Group Loona on New Song "love4eva": Listen|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=May 30, 2018|access-date=July 19, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180617043456/https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-joins-k-pop-group-loona-on-new-song-love4eva-listen|archive-date=June 17, 2018|url-status=live}}</ref> On June 15, 2018, she was featured in a video for [[Apple Inc.|Apple]]'s Behind the Mac series on their YouTube channel, with a preview of a song from her upcoming album titled "That's What the Drugs Are For", later released as "[[My Name Is Dark]]".<ref>{{cite web|first=Sarah|last=Murphy|url=https://exclaim.ca/music/article/grimes_debuts_new_song_thats_what_the_drugs_are_for_in_apple_commercial|title=Grimes Debuts New Song "That's What the Drugs Are For"|work=[[Exclaim!]]|date=June 15, 2018|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022858/https://exclaim.ca/music/article/grimes_debuts_new_song_thats_what_the_drugs_are_for_in_apple_commercial|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first1=Michelle Hyun|last1=Kim|first2=Sam|last2=Sodomsky|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-debuts-new-song-in-apple-commercial-watch|title=Grimes Debuts New Song in Apple Commercial: Watch|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=June 15, 2018|access-date=July 19, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180617043249/https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-debuts-new-song-in-apple-commercial-watch|archive-date=June 17, 2018|url-status=live}}</ref> On the same day, she posted two Twitter videos previewing two songs from her upcoming album, "adore u (beautiful game)" and "4ÆM".<ref>{{cite web|first=Jazz|last=Monroe|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-previews-2-new-songs-listen|title=Pitchfork: Grimes Previews 2 New Songs: Listen|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=June 5, 2018|access-date=June 17, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180616233935/https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-previews-2-new-songs-listen|archive-date=June 16, 2018|url-status=live}}</ref> In 2018, Grimes composed the theme music for [[Netflix]]'s animated series ''[[Hilda (TV series)|Hilda]]''.<ref name="Hilda">{{cite web|first=Charlotte|last=Krol|url=https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-writes-theme-song-for-netflix-series-hilda-listen-2382482|title=Grimes writes theme song for new Netflix series 'Hilda' – listen|work=[[NME]]|date=September 22, 2018|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022856/https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-writes-theme-song-for-netflix-series-hilda-listen-2382482|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Hilda2">{{cite magazine|first=Justin|last=Kamp|url=https://www.pastemagazine.com/music/grimes/everything-we-know-about-grimes-new-album-so-far|title=Everything We Know about Grimes' New Album So Far|magazine=[[Paste (magazine)|Paste]]|date=November 29, 2018|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230930115903/https://www.pastemagazine.com/music/grimes/everything-we-know-about-grimes-new-album-so-far|archive-date=September 30, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> On October 19, 2018, Grimes was featured on [[Jimmy Urine]]'s "The Medicine Does Not Control Me" from the album, ''Euringer''.<ref>{{cite web|first=Lake|last=Schatz|url=https://consequence.net/2018/10/grimes-jimmy-urine-medicine-doesnt-control|title=Grimes joins Mindless Self Indulgence's Jimmy Urine on new song "The Medicine Does Not Control Me": Stream|work=[[Consequence (publication)|Consequence]]|date=October 19, 2018|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220516192050/https://consequence.net/2018/10/grimes-jimmy-urine-medicine-doesnt-control/|archive-date=May 16, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref>

On October 31, 2018, Grimes was featured on "[[Play Destroy]]" by [[Poppy (singer)|Poppy]] on her album ''[[Am I a Girl?]]''<ref>{{cite web|first1=Michelle Hyun|last1=Kim|first2=Evan|last2=Minsker|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-and-poppy-share-new-song-play-destroy-watch|title=Grimes and Poppy Share New Song "Play Destroy": Listen – Pitchfork|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=October 31, 2018|access-date=October 31, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181031135907/https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-and-poppy-share-new-song-play-destroy-watch|archive-date=October 31, 2018|url-status=live}}</ref> Shortly after the release of "Play Destroy", Poppy accused Grimes of bullying during the making of "Play Destroy" stating:
{{Blockquote|"I was kind of bullied into submission by [Grimes] and her team of self-proclaimed feminists", she says. "We planned the song coming out months ago, and she was preventing it. I got to watch her bully songwriters into signing NDA and not taking credit for songs that they were a part of. She doesn't practice what she preaches."<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Anna|last=Gaca|url=https://www.spin.com/2018/11/poppy-says-grimes-bullied-her|title=Poppy Says Grimes "Bullied" Her During the Making of Their Song "Play Destroy"|magazine=[[Spin (magazine)|Spin]]|date=November 30, 2018|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230604095555/https://www.spin.com/2018/11/poppy-says-grimes-bullied-her/|archive-date=June 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
Grimes responded by saying:
{{Blockquote|"Poppy, you dragged me into a disgusting situation and won't stop punishing me for not wanting to be a part of it", Grimes says. "I don't want to work with you, you leaked the song anyway. u got what you want. Let it go."<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.altpress.com/grimes-poppy-responds-bully-play-destroy|title=Grimes says Poppy dragged her into a "disgusting situation"|magazine=[[Alternative Press (magazine)|Alternative Press]]|date=December 2, 2018|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230604095555/https://www.spin.com/2018/11/poppy-says-grimes-bullied-her/|archive-date=June 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>}}

On November 29, 2018, Grimes released the single, "[[We Appreciate Power]]" featuring [[Hana (American musician)|Hana]],<ref name="We Appreciate Power Fact">{{cite magazine|first=Henry|last=Bruce-Jones|url=https://www.factmag.com/2018/11/29/grimes-we-appreciate-power|title=Grimes pushes a pro-AI agenda on industrial rock anthem 'We Appreciate Power'|magazine=[[Fact (UK magazine)|Fact]]|date=November 29, 2018|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230519012048/https://www.factmag.com/2018/11/29/grimes-we-appreciate-power/|archive-date=May 19, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|first=Brendan|last=Klinkenberg|url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/grimes-we-appreciate-power-new-song-761222|title= Hear Grimes' Assertive New Song 'We Appreciate Power'|magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]|date=November 29, 2018|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230331071421/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/grimes-we-appreciate-power-new-song-761222/|archive-date=March 31, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="We Appreciate Power The Guardian">{{cite web|first=Mark|last=Beaumont|url=https://www.theguardian.com/music/2018/dec/07/grimes-new-track-of-week|title=Tracks of the week reviewed: Grimes, Los Unidades, Chance the Rapper|work=[[The Guardian]]|date=December 7, 2018|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022854/https://www.theguardian.com/music/2018/dec/07/grimes-new-track-of-week|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> which was described as an [[industrial rock]]<ref name="We Appreciate Power Fact"/> and [[nu metal]] song.<ref name="We Appreciate Power The Guardian"/> On December 11, 2018, Grimes performed the song on ''[[The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon]]''.<ref>{{cite web|first=Trey|last=Alston|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/watch-grimes-perform-we-appreciate-power-on-fallon|title=Watch Grimes Perform "We Appreciate Power" on "Fallon"|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=December 11, 2018|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230710083628/https://pitchfork.com/news/watch-grimes-perform-we-appreciate-power-on-fallon/|archive-date=July 10, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|first=Christopher|last=Roberts|url=https://www.undertheradarmag.com/news/watch_grimes_perform_we_appreciate_power_on_the_tonight_show_starring_jimmy|title=Watch Grimes Perform "We Appreciate Power" on "The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon" Single Out Now via 4AD; It's the First Taste of Her Fifth Album|magazine=[[Under the Radar (magazine)|Under the Radar]]|date=December 11, 2018|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022855/https://www.undertheradarmag.com/news/watch_grimes_perform_we_appreciate_power_on_the_tonight_show_starring_jimmy|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> Grimes also appeared on [[Bring Me the Horizon]]'s "[[Nihilist Blues]]" from their sixth album, ''[[Amo (Bring Me the Horizon album)|Amo]]''.<ref name="Blabbermouth Nihilist Blues">{{cite web|url=https://blabbermouth.net/news/listen-to-bring-me-the-horizons-collaboration-with-synth-pop-singer-grimes-nihilist-blues|title=Listen To Bring Me The Horizon's Collaboration With Synth-Pop Singer Grimes, 'Nihilist Blues'|work=[[Blabbermouth.net]]|date=January 24, 2019|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230407184930/https://blabbermouth.net/news/listen-to-bring-me-the-horizons-collaboration-with-synth-pop-singer-grimes-nihilist-blues|archive-date=April 7, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Revolver Nihilist Blues">{{cite magazine|first=John|last=Hill|url=https://www.revolvermag.com/music/hear-bring-me-horizon-team-grimes-dark-new-dance-song-nihilist-blues|title=Hear Bring Me the Horizon Team With Grimes on Dark New Dance Song "Nihilist Blues"|magazine=[[Revolver (magazine)|Revolver]]|date=January 24, 2019|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406024357/https://www.revolvermag.com/music/hear-bring-me-horizon-team-grimes-dark-new-dance-song-nihilist-blues|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>

On August 13, 2019, Grimes posted an advertisement for the [[Adidas]] by [[Stella McCartney]] Fall 2019 collection on Instagram, stating that she would release the first single off her upcoming album, ''[[Miss Anthropocene]]'', on September 13, 2019.<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Rania|last=Aniftos|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/grimes-new-single-release-date-adidas-ad-8527346|title=Grimes Announces New Single Release Date in Adidas Ad: Watch|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|date=August 13, 2019|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230204115519/https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/grimes-new-single-release-date-adidas-ad-8527346/|archive-date=February 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Chloe|last=Gilke|url=https://uproxx.com/indie/grimes-miss-anthropocene-single-adidas-advertisement|title=Grimes Teased Her First 'Miss Anthropocene' Single In A New Adidas Advertisement|work=[[Uproxx]]|date=August 13, 2019|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230606132850/https://uproxx.com/indie/grimes-miss-anthropocene-single-adidas-advertisement/|archive-date=June 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> She released the music video for "[[Violence (song)|Violence]]", featuring [[I_o_(musician)|i_o]], on September 5, 2019.<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Jem|last=Aswad|url=https://variety.com/2019/music/news/grimes-drops-new-single-and-video-violence-1203324574|title=Grimes Drops New Single and Video, 'Violence'|magazine=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|date=September 5, 2019|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230901235529/https://variety.com/2019/music/news/grimes-drops-new-single-and-video-violence-1203324574/|archive-date=September 1, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|first=Winston|last=Cook-Wilson|url=https://www.spin.com/2019/09/grimes-i_o-violence-video-watch|title=Grimes Releases Video for New Song "Violence": Watch|magazine=[[Spin (magazine)|Spin]]|date=September 5, 2019|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004154229/https://www.spin.com/2019/09/grimes-i_o-violence-video-watch/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> On October 25, 2019, an unfinished version of the album was leaked online.<ref>{{cite web|first=Samuel|last=Regan|url=https://hasitleaked.com/2019/grimes-miss_anthropocene|title=Grimes: Miss_Anthropocene|website=hasitleaked.com|date=October 26, 2019|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004131941/https://hasitleaked.com/2019/grimes-miss_anthropocene/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> On November 15, 2019, she released two versions of the single "So Heavy I Fell Through the Earth"<ref>{{cite web|first=Will|last=Richards|url=https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-to-release-new-song-so-heavy-this-week-2574613|title=Listen to two versions of Grimes' booming new song 'So Heavy I Fell Through The Earth'|work=[[NME]]|date=November 15, 2019|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022858/https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-to-release-new-song-so-heavy-this-week-2574613|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Andrew|last=Sacher|url=http://www.brooklynvegan.com/grimes-shares-new-song-so-heavy-i-fell-through-the-earth/?trackback=tsmclip|title=Grimes shares "So Heavy I Fell Through the Earth," reveals album details|work=[[BrooklynVegan]]|date=November 15, 2019|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230407184930/http://www.brooklynvegan.com/grimes-shares-new-song-so-heavy-i-fell-through-the-earth/?trackback=tsmclip|archive-date=April 7, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> and performed "4ÆM" at the 2019 Video Game Awards in order to introduce herself as Lizzy Wizzy, a voiced character in the game [[Cyberpunk 2077]].<ref name="Cyberpunk 2077 1">{{cite web|first=Chris|last=DeVille|url=https://www.stereogum.com/2067774/grimes-4aem-game-awards-lizzy-wizzy-cyberpunk-2077/music|title=Grimes Debuts "4ÆM" At The Game Awards, Will Portray Pop Star Lizzy Wizzy In Cyberpunk 2077|work=[[Stereogum]]|date=December 12, 2019|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230512220427/https://www.stereogum.com/2067774/grimes-4aem-game-awards-lizzy-wizzy-cyberpunk-2077/music/|archive-date=May 12, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Cyberpunk 2077 2">{{cite web|first=Matthew|last=Strauss|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/watch-grimes-perform-new-song-4aem-at-2020-game-awards|title=Watch Grimes Perform New Song "4ÆM" at 2020 Game Awards|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=December 12, 2019|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230518185044/https://pitchfork.com/news/watch-grimes-perform-new-song-4aem-at-2020-game-awards/|archive-date=May 18, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> On November 29, 2019, Grimes released the single "My Name Is Dark".<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Shaad|last=D'Souza|url=https://www.thefader.com/2019/11/29/grimes-drops-new-track-my-name-is-dark|title=Grimes drops new track "My Name Is Dark"|magazine=[[The Fader]]|date=November 29, 2019|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022854/https://www.thefader.com/2019/11/29/grimes-drops-new-track-my-name-is-dark|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Peter|last=Helman|url=https://www.stereogum.com/2066424/grimes-my-name-is-dark/music|title=Grimes – "My Name Is Dark"|work=[[Stereogum]]|date=November 29, 2019|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230513004125/https://www.stereogum.com/2066424/grimes-my-name-is-dark/music/|archive-date=May 13, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> On December 13, 2019, Grimes released the single "4ÆM".<ref>{{cite web|first=Robin|last=Murray|url=https://www.clashmusic.com/news/listen-grimes-4aem|title=Listen: Grimes – '4ÆM'|work=[[Clash (magazine)|Clash]]|date=December 13, 2019|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230709173342/https://www.clashmusic.com/news/listen-grimes-4aem|archive-date=July 9, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Cerys|last=Kenneally|url=https://www.thelineofbestfit.com/news/latest-news/grimes-teases-new-single-4aem-dropping-today|title=Grimes teases new single "4ÆM" dropping today|work=[[The Line of Best Fit]]|date=December 12, 2019|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022854/https://www.thelineofbestfit.com/news/latest-news/grimes-teases-new-single-4aem-dropping-today|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> ''Miss Anthropocene'' was released on February 21, 2020.<ref>{{cite web|first=Heather|last=Phares|url=https://www.allmusic.com/album/miss-anthropocene-mw0003337691|title=Miss Anthropocene – Grimes|work=[[AllMusic]]|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022854/https://www.allmusic.com/album/miss-anthropocene-mw0003337691|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Barry|last=Nicolson|url=https://www.nme.com/reviews/grimes-miss-anthropocene-review-2612446|title=Grimes – 'Miss Anthropocene'|work=[[NME]]|date=February 21, 2020|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230331141011/https://www.nme.com/reviews/grimes-miss-anthropocene-review-2612446|archive-date=March 31, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> On February 12, 2020, she released the single "[[Delete Forever]]", which was partly inspired by the death of [[Lil Peep]] and the [[Opioid epidemic in the United States|ongoing opioid crisis]].<ref>{{Cite magazine|first=Claire|last=Shaffer|url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/grimes-delete-forever-lil-peep-951653|title=Grimes Says New Song 'Delete Forever' Was Inspired by Lil Peep's Death|magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]|date=February 12, 2020|access-date=July 19, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220322054639/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/grimes-delete-forever-lil-peep-951653|archive-date=March 22, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|first=Joe|last=Coscarelli|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/20/arts/music/grimes-delete-forever.html|title=How Grimes, the Ultimate D.I.Y. Pop Star, Made 'Delete Forever'|work=[[The New York Times]]|date=March 20, 2020|access-date=July 19, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200320041032/https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/20/arts/music/grimes-delete-forever.html|archive-date=March 20, 2020|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=James|last=Rettig|url=https://www.stereogum.com/2073380/grimes-delete-forever/music|title=Grimes – "Delete Forever"|work=[[Stereogum]]|date=February 12, 2020|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230606053142/https://www.stereogum.com/2073380/grimes-delete-forever/music/|archive-date=June 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> On February 27, 2020, Grimes released a music video for the song "Idoru".<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Shaad|last=D'Souza|url=https://www.thefader.com/2020/02/27/grimes-drops-new-videos-for-idoru-miss-anthropocene-2020|title=Grimes drops new videos for "Idoru"|magazine=[[The Fader]]|date=February 27, 2020|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022855/https://www.thefader.com/2020/02/27/grimes-drops-new-videos-for-idoru-miss-anthropocene-2020|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Wren|last=Graves|url=https://consequence.net/2020/02/stream-grimes-music-video-idoru|title=Grimes Shares New Music Video for "Idoru": Stream|work=[[Consequence (publication)|Consequence]]|date=February 27, 2020|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004154221/https://consequence.net/2020/02/stream-grimes-music-video-idoru/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> On April 1, 2020, Grimes released a music video for the song "You'll Miss Me When I'm Not Around" and asked fans to finish the video because it only features Grimes and a green screen.<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Heran|last=Mamo|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/grimes-youll-miss-me-when-im-not-around-video-9348765|title=Grimes Asks Fans to Collaborate on 'You'll Miss Me When I'm Not Around' Video|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|date=April 1, 2020|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004132410/https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/grimes-youll-miss-me-when-im-not-around-video-9348765/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Trey|last=Alston|url=https://www.mtv.com/news/dms8gx/grimes-youll-miss-me-when-im-not-around-video-chroma-green|title=Grimes Shares 'You'll Miss Me When I'm Not Around' Video|work=[[MTV News]]|date=April 1, 2020|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406024357/https://www.mtv.com/news/dms8gx/grimes-youll-miss-me-when-im-not-around-video-chroma-green|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=dead}}</ref> On June 17, 2020, Grimes was featured on [[Ashnikko]]'s song, "[[Cry (Ashnikko song)|Cry]]" from her mixtape, ''[[Demidevil]]''.<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Heran|last=Mamo|url=https://www.billboard.com/articles/news/9404377/ashnikko-grimes-cry-music-video|title=Grimes Returns With First New Music Post-Baby in Ashnikko's 'Cry' Action-Packed Anime Video|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|date=June 17, 2020|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201101195758/https://www.billboard.com/articles/news/9404377/ashnikko-grimes-cry-music-video|archive-date=November 1, 2020|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Peter|last=Helman|url=https://www.stereogum.com/2088051/ashnikko-cry-feat-grimes/music|title=Ashnikko – "Cry" (Feat. Grimes)|work=[[Stereogum]]|date=June 17, 2020|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200618020008/https://www.stereogum.com/2088051/ashnikko-cry-feat-grimes/music/|archive-date=June 18, 2020|url-status=live}}</ref>

Grimes made an appearance on the [[Adult Swim]] [[sketch comedy]] show, ''[[The Eric Andre Show]]''.<ref name="The Eric Andre Show">{{cite web|first=Matthew|last=Ismael Ruiz|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/watch-grimes-get-tortured-on-the-eric-andre-show|title=Watch Grimes Get "Tortured" on The Eric Andre Show|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=November 10, 2020|access-date=December 9, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230513104424/https://pitchfork.com/news/watch-grimes-get-tortured-on-the-eric-andre-show/|archive-date=May 13, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="The Eric Andre Show2">{{cite magazine|first=Shaad|last=DsouzaRuiz|url=https://www.thefader.com/2020/11/11/watch-grimes-get-tortured-cheeseboarded-on-the-eric-andre-show|title=Watch Grimes get tortured, "cheeseboarded" on The Eric Andre Show|magazine=[[The Fader]]|date=November 11, 2020|access-date=December 9, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220814114815/https://www.thefader.com/2020/11/11/watch-grimes-get-tortured-cheeseboarded-on-the-eric-andre-show|archive-date=August 14, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref> Her collaboration with [[Janelle Monáe]], "[[Pynk]]", was featured on episode 5 of the television series, ''[[I May Destroy You]]''.<ref name="I May Destroy You">{{cite web|first=Amanda|last=Dobbins|url=https://www.vulture.com/article/i-may-destroy-you-soundtrack-songs-analysis-playlist.html|title=Michaela Coel Always Knew How She Wanted I May Destroy You to Sound|work=[[Vulture (blog)|Vulture]]|date=August 24, 2020|access-date=August 9, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220224101854/https://www.vulture.com/article/i-may-destroy-you-soundtrack-songs-analysis-playlist.html|archive-date=February 24, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref> Her song "[[Oblivion (Grimes song)|Oblivion]]" was featured on episode 9 of the same series.<ref name="I May Destroy You"/> Grimes collaborated with [[Benee]] on the dance-style song "Sheesh" on the latter's debut album, ''[[Hey U X]]'', released on November 11, 2020.<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Bella|last=Martin|url=https://diymag.com/2020/11/12/benee-hey-u-x-album-review|title=Benee – Hey u x|magazine=[[DIY (magazine)|DIY]]|date=November 13, 2020|access-date=December 9, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220322054803/https://diymag.com/2020/11/12/benee-hey-u-x-album-review|archive-date=March 22, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref> Her song, "Kill V Maim" was featured in the soundtrack of the 2020 film, ''[[Mainstream (film)|Mainstream]]''.<ref>{{cite web|first=Isaac|last=Feldberg|url=https://www.rogerebert.com/reviews/mainstream-movie-review-2021|title=Mainstream|work=rogerebert.com|date=May 7, 2021|access-date=December 9, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406024358/https://www.rogerebert.com/reviews/mainstream-movie-review-2021|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> On December 11, 2020, Grimes and other associated artists, all using aliases, released a ''Cyberpunk 2077''-themed DJ mix album on [[Apple Music]], titled ''This story is dedicated to all those cyberpunks who fight against injustice and corruption every day of their lives!''. It contains two new songs by Grimes, "Samana" and "Delicate Weapon".<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://crackmagazine.net/2020/12/grimes-surprise-releases-dj-mix-album|title=Grimes surprise-releases DJ mix album|magazine=[[Crack (magazine)|Crack]]|date=December 11, 2020|access-date=December 9, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230326224142/https://crackmagazine.net/2020/12/grimes-surprise-releases-dj-mix-album/|archive-date=March 26, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Will|last=Richards|url=https://www.nme.com/news/music/listen-to-grimes-new-song-delicate-weapon-from-cyberpunk-2077-soundtrack-2837313|title=Listen to Grimes' new song 'Delicate Weapon' from 'Cyberpunk 2077' soundtrack|work=[[NME]]|date=December 12, 2020|access-date=December 9, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022900/https://www.nme.com/news/music/listen-to-grimes-new-song-delicate-weapon-from-cyberpunk-2077-soundtrack-2837313|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> On December 18, 2020, nine months after the release of her fifth studio album, ''Miss Anthropocene'', Grimes changed the cover art for the album on all streaming platforms.<ref name="Replacement cover art">{{cite web|first=Matthew|last=Strauss|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-changes-miss-anthropocene-album-cover|title=Grimes Changes Miss Anthropocene Album Cover|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=December 18, 2020|access-date=December 9, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230513014423/https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-changes-miss-anthropocene-album-cover/|archive-date=May 13, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Replacement cover art2">{{cite web|first=Nina|last=Corcoran|url=https://consequence.net/2020/12/grimes-miss-anthropocene-cover-art|title=Grimes Changes the Album Artwork for Miss Anthropocene|work=[[Consequence (publication)|Consequence]]|date=December 18, 2020|access-date=December 9, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230513045004/https://consequence.net/2020/12/grimes-miss-anthropocene-cover-art/|archive-date=May 13, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> The new cover art is a painting by Rupid Leejm that Grimes commissioned to use.<ref name="Replacement cover art"/><ref name="Replacement cover art2"/> In discussing the process of choosing the cover art originally, "I polled a bunch of ppl and everyone said not to use it (??) but I wish I trusted my gut. I fucking LOVE this painting."<ref name="Replacement cover art"/><ref name="Replacement cover art2"/> On January 1, 2021, Grimes released ''Miss Anthropocene: Rave Edition'', a [[remix album]] featuring new versions of songs on the album by artists including [[BloodPop]], [[Channel Tres]], [[Richie Hawtin]], and [[Modeselektor]], along with two remixes from her ''[[Cyberpunk 2077]]'' [[Apple Music]] [[DJ mix]].<ref>{{cite web|first=Alex|last=Hudson|url=https://exclaim.ca/music/article/grimes_to_release_miss_anthropocene_remix_album|title=Grimes to Release 'Miss Anthropocene' Remix Album|work=[[Exclaim!]]|date=December 29, 2020|access-date=December 9, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022903/https://exclaim.ca/music/article/grimes_to_release_miss_anthropocene_remix_album|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Thom|last=Waite|url=https://www.dazeddigital.com/music/article/51536/1/grimes-announces-new-remix-album-miss-anthropocene-rave-edition-bloodpop|title=Grimes announces a new remix album, Miss Anthropocene Rave Edition|work=[[Dazed]]|date=December 29, 2020|access-date=August 2, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201231075717/https://www.dazeddigital.com/music/article/51536/1/grimes-announces-new-remix-album-miss-anthropocene-rave-edition-bloodpop|archive-date=December 31, 2020|url-status=live}}</ref>

=== 2021–present: ''Alter Ego'', collaborations, and upcoming sixth album ===
On March 5, 2021, Grimes signed with [[Columbia Records]].<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Stephen|last=Ackroyd|url=https://readdork.com/news/grimes-columbia-records|title=Grimes has reportedly made the major label switch, signing to Columbia Records|magazine=[[Dork (magazine)|Dork]]|date=March 6, 2021|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230327124624/https://readdork.com/news/grimes-columbia-records/|archive-date=March 27, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Brock|last=Thiessen|url=https://exclaim.ca/music/article/grimes_signs_to_columbia_records_report|title=Grimes Signs to Columbia Records|work=[[Exclaim!]]|date=March 8, 2021|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022906/https://exclaim.ca/music/article/grimes_signs_to_columbia_records_report|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|first=Colin|last=Stutz|url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/grimes-columbia-records-deal/|title=Grimes Signs to Columbia Records: Exclusive|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|date=March 5, 2021|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230409125158/https://www.billboard.com/pro/grimes-columbia-records-deal/|archive-date=April 9, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> On May 8, Grimes appeared on a ''[[Saturday Night Live]]'' sketch as [[Princess Peach]] alongside the host, [[Elon Musk]], as [[Wario]].<ref name="SNL">{{cite magazine|first=Mitchell|last=Peters|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/grimes-snl-princess-peach-elon-musk-wario-video-9569601|title=Grimes Nails it as Princess Peach Alongside Elon Musk as Wario in 'SNL' Super Mario Murder Trial Skit: Watch|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|date=May 9, 2021|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004131731/https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/grimes-snl-princess-peach-elon-musk-wario-video-9569601/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> Her song "California" was featured in the animated film ''[[The Mitchells vs. the Machines]]''.<ref>{{cite web|first=Q.V.|last=Hough|url=https://screenrant.com/mitchells-vs-machines-soundtrack-guide-every-song|title=The Mitchells vs. The Machines Soundtrack Guide: Every Song|work=[[Screen Rant]]|date=April 30, 2021|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220413174337/https://screenrant.com/mitchells-vs-machines-soundtrack-guide-every-song/|archive-date=April 13, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref> In June, she appeared in [[Doja Cat]]'s music video "[[Need to Know (Doja Cat song)|Need to Know]]".<ref>{{cite web|first=Gabrielle|last=Sanchez|url=https://www.avclub.com/grimes-preparing-for-her-life-on-mars-with-elon-probab-1847082559|title=Grimes, preparing for her life on Mars with Elon probably, appears as an alien in Doja Cat's new video|work=[[The A.V. Club]]|date=June 11, 2021|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230708080424/https://www.avclub.com/grimes-preparing-for-her-life-on-mars-with-elon-probab-1847082559|archive-date=July 8, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Glenn|last=Rowley|url=https://consequence.net/2021/06/doja-cat-debuts-need-to-know-with-grimes-featuring-music-video-watch|title=Doja Cat Debuts "Need to Know" with Grimes-Featuring Music Video: Watch|work=[[Consequence (publication)|Consequence]]|date=June 11, 2021|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004132514/https://consequence.net/2021/06/doja-cat-debuts-need-to-know-with-grimes-featuring-music-video-watch/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>

Later in June, Grimes started a new partnered [[Discord (software)|Discord]] server called "Grimes Metaverse Super Beta" and a new podcast "Homo Techno", co-hosted with science communicator [[Liv Boeree]].<ref name="Shinigami Eyes">{{cite web|first=Layla|last=Halabian|url=https://www.nylon.com/life/grimes-podcast-homo-techno-shinigami-eyes-discord|title=Grimes To Launch Podcast, Teases New Song "Shinigami Eyes"|work=[[Nylon (magazine)|Nylon]]|date=June 21, 2021|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022855/https://www.nylon.com/life/grimes-podcast-homo-techno-shinigami-eyes-discord|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> She used the Discord server to tease new music frequently, and released a snippet of a song called "Shinigami Eyes" which she continued to promote in subsequent social media posts,<ref name="Shinigami Eyes"/> as well as an upcoming collaboration with British DJ [[Chris Lake]].<ref>{{cite web|first=Charlotte|last=Krol|url=https://www.nme.com/en_au/news/music/grimes-shares-clip-of-new-chris-lake-collaboration-2953593|title=Grimes shares clip of new Chris Lake collaboration|work=[[NME]]|date=June 1, 2021|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022855/https://www.nme.com/en_au/news/music/grimes-shares-clip-of-new-chris-lake-collaboration-2953593|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> Grimes spoke about an upcoming concept album with Billboard, describing it as a "space opera".<ref name="Discord: The Movie">{{cite magazine|first=Tatiana|last=Cirisano|url=https://www.billboard.com/articles/news/dance/9605347/grimes-interview-discord-new-album-futurism|title=Grimes on Discord, Her 'Space Opera' & Being Right About the Future: 'I'm Not Just Trying to Be Weird'|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|date=July 23, 2021|access-date=July 26, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220322054640/https://www.billboard.com/pro/grimes-interview-discord-new-album-futurism|archive-date=March 22, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref>

In July 2021, Grimes, alongside [[will.i.am]], [[Alanis Morissette]], [[Nick Lachey]], and [[Rocsi Diaz]] were revealed as judges on ''[[Alter Ego (TV series)|Alter Ego]]'', a new singing competition series in which the contestants make the use of motion capture technology to portray themselves as "dream avatars".<ref name="Alter Ego">{{Cite web|first=Noah|last=Yoo|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-alanis-morissette-william-to-judge-new-avatar-singing-competition-tv-show|title=Grimes, Alanis Morissette, and Will.i.am to Judge New "Avatar Singing Competition" TV Show|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=July 16, 2021|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230528064609/https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-alanis-morissette-william-to-judge-new-avatar-singing-competition-tv-show/|archive-date=May 28, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Alter Ego2">{{cite web|first=Kelly|last=Lawler|url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/tv/2021/09/08/grimes-alter-ego-and-pressure-physically-beautiful/5774808001|title=Grimes talks her new show 'Alter Ego' and feeling 'pressure to be physically beautiful'|work=[[USA Today]]|date=September 8, 2021|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004132028/https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/tv/2021/09/08/grimes-alter-ego-and-pressure-physically-beautiful/5774808001/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> She also made a cameo appearance in the short film ''Discord: The Movie'', alongside [[Awkwafina]], [[Danny DeVito]], and [[J Balvin]].<ref name="Discord: The Movie"/><ref name="Discord: The Movie2">{{cite web|first=Caitlin|last=White|url=https://uproxx.com/music/awkwafina-danny-devito-discord-movie-grimes-j-balvin|title=Awkwafina And Danny DeVito Take A Wild Ride Through The Internet In 'Discord: The Movie'|work=[[Uproxx]]|date=July 23, 2021|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004133059/https://uproxx.com/music/awkwafina-danny-devito-discord-movie-grimes-j-balvin/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> On September 30, Grimes released a new song titled "Love" recorded in response to her separation from Elon Musk and its subsequent media attention.<ref name="Love">{{cite magazine|first=Heran|last=Mamo|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/grimes-love-song-elon-musk-breakup-9638782/|title=Grimes Shares New Song 'Love' in Response to 'Harassment by Paparazzis' After Elon Musk Split|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|date=September 30, 2021|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220519164015/https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/grimes-love-song-elon-musk-breakup-9638782/amp/|archive-date=May 19, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Love2">{{cite web|first=Sam|last=Moore|url=https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-shares-her-brand-new-song-love-on-instagram-3059409|title=Grimes shares her brand new song 'Love' on Instagram|work=[[NME]]|date=September 30, 2021|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022902/https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-shares-her-brand-new-song-love-on-instagram-3059409|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> On December 3, Grimes announced the title of her sixth studio album, ''Book 1'', and released a new single titled "Player of Games".<ref name="TLOBF Book1">{{cite web|first=Cerys|last=Kenneally|url=https://www.thelineofbestfit.com/news/latest-news/grimes-begins-book-1-era-with-new-single-player-of-games|title=Grimes begins Book 1 era with new single "Player of Games"|work=[[The Line of Best Fit]]|date=December 3, 2021|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022855/https://www.thelineofbestfit.com/news/latest-news/grimes-begins-book-1-era-with-new-single-player-of-games|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Evan|last=Minsker|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-shares-new-song-player-of-games-listen|title=Grimes Shares New Song "Player of Games": Listen|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=December 3, 2021|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230327112619/https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-shares-new-song-player-of-games-listen/|archive-date=March 27, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> In December, Grimes teased a collaboration with [[the Weeknd]] on Discord, saying it would be released in 2022.<ref name="thelineofbestfit The Weeknd">{{cite web|first=Cerys|last=Kenneally|url=https://www.thelineofbestfit.com/news/grimes-collaboration-with-the-weeknd-will-reportedly-arrive-this-summer|title=Grimes' collaboration with The Weeknd will reportedly arrive this summer|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=August 16, 2022|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022857/https://www.thelineofbestfit.com/news/grimes-collaboration-with-the-weeknd-will-reportedly-arrive-this-summer|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="NME The Weeknd">{{cite web|first=Rhian|last=Daly|url=https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-the-weeknd-collaboration-on-way-soon-sci-fi-3291365|title=Grimes' The Weeknd collaboration is reportedly on the way soon|work=[[NME]]|date=August 16, 2022|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022855/https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-the-weeknd-collaboration-on-way-soon-sci-fi-3291365|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>

In January 2022, Grimes partnered with the video game [[Rocket League]] for the Neon Nights event.<ref name="Gamespot Rocket League">{{cite web|first=Eddie|last=Makuch|url=https://www.gamespot.com/articles/rocket-league-is-teaming-up-with-grimes-for-a-special-crossover-event/1100-6499821|title=Rocket League Is Teaming Up With Grimes For A Special Crossover Event|work=[[GameSpot]]|date=January 20, 2022|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004134317/https://www.gamespot.com/articles/rocket-league-is-teaming-up-with-grimes-for-a-special-crossover-event/1100-6499821/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="NME Rocket League">{{cite web|first=Georgina|last=Young|url=https://www.nme.com/news/gaming-news/rocket-leagues-grimes-neon-nights-event-has-begun-3147149|title='Rocket League's Grimes Neon Nights event has begun|work=[[NME]]|date=January 26, 2022|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406024406/https://www.nme.com/news/gaming-news/rocket-leagues-grimes-neon-nights-event-has-begun-3147149|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> The event ran from January 26 to February 8, and featured Grimes-themed items and her songs "Shinigami Eyes" and "Player of Games".<ref name="Gamespot Rocket League"/><ref name="NME Rocket League"/> In January, Grimes announced a 10th anniversary vinyl of her album ''Visions''.<ref>{{cite web|first=Nina|last=Corcoran|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-announces-10th-anniversary-reissue-of-visions|title=Grimes Announces 10th Anniversary Reissue of Visions|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=January 20, 2022|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004131741/https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-announces-10th-anniversary-reissue-of-visions/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> On January 26, she released "Shinigami Eyes".<ref>{{cite web|first=Rhian|last=Daly|url=https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-new-song-shinigami-eyes-3147114|title=Grimes shares manga-inspired new song 'Shinigami Eyes'|work=[[NME]]|date=January 26, 2022|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022856/https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-new-song-shinigami-eyes-3147114|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Fairies Cum First Pitchfork">{{Cite web|first=Matthew|last=Strauss|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-shares-video-for-new-song-shinigami-eyes-watch|title=Grimes Shares Video for New Song "Shinigami Eyes"|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=January 26, 2022|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230315044532/https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-shares-video-for-new-song-shinigami-eyes-watch/|archive-date=March 15, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> A week later, on February 3, 2022, Grimes announced her forthcoming EP titled ''Fairies Cum First''.<ref name="Fairies Cum First Pitchfork" /><ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://diymag.com/2022/02/04/grimes-new-fairies-cum-first-ep|title=Grimes announces 'Fairies Cum First' EP|magazine=[[DIY (magazine)|DIY]]|date=February 4, 2022|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406225252/https://diymag.com/news/grimes-new-fairies-cum-first-ep|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> In April, Grimes was featured on the song, "Last Day" by the Russian band [[IC3PEAK]] from the album ''Kiss of Death''.<ref name="IC3PEAK">{{cite web|first=Glenn|last=Rowley|url=https://consequence.net/2022/04/grimes-ic3peak-last-day-stream|title=Grimes Joins Russian Band IC3PEAK on New Single "Last Day / Новый день": Stream|work=[[Consequence (publication)|Consequence]]|date=April 22, 2022|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220803043958/https://consequence.net/2022/04/grimes-ic3peak-last-day-stream/|archive-date=August 3, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref> Grimes was featured in the music video for [[Bella Poarch]]'s "Dolls" which was released on July 15.<ref>{{cite web|first=Matthew|last=Strauss|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-stars-in-bella-poarch-video-for-new-song-dolls-watch|title=Grimes Stars in Bella Poarch's Video for New Song "Dolls": Watch|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=July 15, 2022|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230327032512/https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-stars-in-bella-poarch-video-for-new-song-dolls-watch/|archive-date=March 27, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|first=Jazz|last=Tangcay|url=https://variety.com/2022/music/news/bella-poarch-dolls-video-1235317748|title=Bella Poarch on Her New Single 'Dolls': 'It's About Not Letting Bullies Get To You'|magazine=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|date=July 15, 2022|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004132511/https://variety.com/2022/music/news/bella-poarch-dolls-video-1235317748/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|first=Tomás|last=Mier|url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-features/bella-poarch-dolls-music-video-1383452|title= That Time Grimes Hit Bella Poarch in the Face|magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]|date=July 15, 2021|access-date=July 24, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220715171018/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-features/bella-poarch-dolls-music-video-1383452|archive-date=July 15, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref> Grimes was an opening act on select dates for [[Swedish House Mafia]]'s "Paradise Again Tour"<ref>{{cite web|first=Grant|last=Albert|url=https://www.miaminewtimes.com/music/review-swedish-house-mafia-paradise-again-tour-at-ftx-arena-july-29-2022-14973389|title=Swedish House Mafia Connected the Dots at FTX Arena, Leaving a Mark for the World|work=[[Miami New Times]]|date=July 30, 2022|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406025859/https://www.miaminewtimes.com/music/review-swedish-house-mafia-paradise-again-tour-at-ftx-arena-july-29-2022-14973389|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> alongside [[Kaytranada]], [[Zhu (musician)|ZHU]], and [[Alesso]].<ref name="IC3PEAK" /><ref name="Paradise Again Tour">{{cite web|url=https://consequence.net/2022/04/swedish-house-mafia-tour-grimes-kaytranda|title=Swedish House Mafia Expand Tour, Announce Grimes and Kaytranada as Opening Acts|work=[[Consequence (publication)|Consequence]]|date=April 18, 2022|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004154548/https://consequence.net/2022/04/swedish-house-mafia-tour-grimes-kaytranda/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> The tour ran from July 29 to November 13<ref name="IC3PEAK" /><ref name="Paradise Again Tour" /> Grimes appeared on Bella Poarch's song, "No Man's Land" from the ''Dolls'' EP, which was released on August 12.<ref>{{cite web|first=Rachel|last=Brodsky|url=https://www.stereogum.com/2195953/bella-poarch-no-mans-land-feat-grimes/music|title=Bella Poarch – "No Man's Land" (Feat. Grimes)|work=[[Stereogum]]|date=August 12, 2022|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220812175604/https://www.stereogum.com/2195953/bella-poarch-no-mans-land-feat-grimes/music/|archive-date=August 12, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|first=Jordan|last=Darville|url=https://www.thefader.com/2022/08/12/grimes-bella-poarch-no-mans-land|title=Grimes features on the new Bella Poarch song "No Man's Land"|magazine=[[The Fader]]|date=August 12, 2022|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022855/https://www.thefader.com/2022/08/12/grimes-bella-poarch-no-mans-land|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>

In August 2022, Grimes was featured on the cover of ''[[Vogue China|Vogue Plus China]]'',<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.designscene.net/2022/08/grimes-vogue-plus-china.html|title=Grimes is the Cover Star of Vogue Plus China|work=Design Scene|date=August 16, 2022|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406024359/https://www.designscene.net/2022/08/grimes-vogue-plus-china.html|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> in which she did an interview and further discussed her upcoming collaboration with The Weeknd.<ref name="thelineofbestfit The Weeknd"/><ref name="NME The Weeknd"/> She confirmed that the song is called "Sci Fi" and is set for release in mid-2022.<ref name="thelineofbestfit The Weeknd"/><ref name="NME The Weeknd"/> She also provided more details about her upcoming studio album and EP, stating, "all these projects [will] come together and merge into one project at the end."<ref name="thelineofbestfit The Weeknd"/><ref name="NME The Weeknd"/> On September 17, she revealed that she has twenty songs for her upcoming album and teased that the album might be divided into two albums.<ref name="September 17, 2022">{{cite web|first=Bryan|last=Kress|url=https://consequence.net/2022/09/grimes-elf-ears-surgery/|title=Grimes Completes New Album After Possibly Undergoing Elf Ears Surgery|work=[[Consequence (publication)|Consequence]]|date=September 18, 2022|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230519143140/https://consequence.net/2022/09/grimes-elf-ears-surgery/|archive-date=May 19, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> She also confirmed that the album was in the process of being mixed.<ref name="September 17, 2022"/> In January 2023, Grimes gave an update on her delayed sixth album, ''Book 1'', announcing that her career was a 'side quest' now and that her children, friends and family were her priorities.<ref name="Music Is My Side Quest Now">{{cite web|first=Megan|last=LaPierre|url=https://exclaim.ca/music/article/grimes_delays_new_album_music_is_my_side_quest_now|title=Grimes Delays New Album: "Music Is My Side Quest Now"|work=[[Exclaim!]]|date=January 4, 2023|access-date=December 11, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230301222628/https://exclaim.ca/music/article/grimes_delays_new_album_music_is_my_side_quest_now|archive-date=March 1, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|first=Glenn|last=Rowley|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/grimes-calls-music-her-side-quest-new-album-update-1235193964/|title=Grimes Calls Music Her 'Side Quest' While Offering Update on Delayed Album|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|date=January 4, 2023|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230423205459/https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/grimes-calls-music-her-side-quest-new-album-update-1235193964/|archive-date=April 23, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Alex|last=Gallagher|url=https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-update-new-album-book-1-says-music-side-quest-3374707|title=Grimes gives update on new music: "Do I want the attention an album brings?|work=[[NME]]|date=January 5, 2023|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230602023113/https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-update-new-album-book-1-says-music-side-quest-3374707|archive-date=June 2, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> On January 31, was announced that Grimes would feature on [[Caroline Polachek]]'s song "Fly to You", alongside [[Dido (singer)|Dido]]. The song is from Polachek's fourth studio album, ''[[Desire, I Want to Turn Into You]]'', which released on February 14.<ref>{{cite web|first=Hollie|last=Geraghty|url=https://www.nme.com/news/music/caroline-polacheks-announces-collaboration-with-grimes-and-dido-on-new-album-3389962|title=Caroline Polachek announces collaboration with Grimes and Dido on new album|work=[[NME]]|date=January 31, 2023|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230301011547/https://www.nme.com/news/music/caroline-polacheks-announces-collaboration-with-grimes-and-dido-on-new-album-3389962|archive-date=March 1, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|first=David|last=Renshaw|url=https://www.thefader.com/2023/01/31/caroline-polachek-blood-and-butter|title=Caroline Polachek shares new song "Blood and Butter," confirms Grimes and Dido collaboration|magazine=[[The Fader]]|date=January 31, 2023|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230329185103/https://www.thefader.com/2023/01/31/caroline-polachek-blood-and-butter|archive-date=March 29, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>

In April 2023, Grimes invited people to use her voice in AI generated songs, stating that she likes the idea of 'killing copyright'.<ref>{{cite web|first=Sian|last=Cain|url=https://www.theguardian.com/music/2023/apr/26/grimes-invites-people-to-use-her-voice-in-ai-songs|title=Grimes invites people to use her voice in AI songs|work=[[The Guardian]]|date=April 26, 2023|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230426025125/https://www.theguardian.com/music/2023/apr/26/grimes-invites-people-to-use-her-voice-in-ai-songs|archive-date=April 26, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Mark|last=Savage|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/entertainment-arts-65385382|title=Grimes says anyone can use her voice for AI-generated songs|work=[[BBC]]|date=April 25, 2023|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230425114417/https://www.bbc.com/news/entertainment-arts-65385382|archive-date=April 25, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> On June 8, Grimes released "Welcome to the Opera", along with Anyma, also known as Matteo Milleri of the Italian duo [[Tale of Us]].<ref>{{cite web|first=Matthew|last=Strauss|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/anyma-and-grimes-share-new-song-welcome-to-the-opera-listen/|title=Anyma and Grimes Share New Song "Welcome to the Opera": Listen|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=June 8, 2023|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230614210835/https://pitchfork.com/news/anyma-and-grimes-share-new-song-welcome-to-the-opera-listen/|archive-date=June 14, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Rachel|last=Brodsky|url=https://www.stereogum.com/2226434/anyma-grimes-welcome-to-the-opera/music/|title=Anyma & Grimes – "Welcome To The Opera"|work=[[Stereogum]]|date=June 8, 2023|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230609014857/https://www.stereogum.com/2226434/anyma-grimes-welcome-to-the-opera/music/|archive-date=June 9, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> On July 28, Grimes released "I Wanna Be Software", with Canadian record producer, [[Illangelo]].<ref>{{cite web|first=Jazz|last=Monroe|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-shares-i-wanna-be-software-listen/|title=Grimes Shares New Song "I Wanna Be Software": Listen|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=July 28, 2023|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230804034506/https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-shares-i-wanna-be-software-listen/|archive-date=August 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Rachel|last=Brodsky|url=https://www.stereogum.com/2231480/grimes-i-wanna-be-software/music/|title=Grimes – "I Wanna Be Software"|work=[[Stereogum]]|date=July 28, 2023|access-date=December 8, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230801051758/https://www.stereogum.com/2231480/grimes-i-wanna-be-software/music/|archive-date=August 1, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> On November 3, Grimes collaborated with Iranian-Dutch singer, [[Sevdaliza]], on the song, "Nothing Lasts Forever".<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Emily|last=Zemler|url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/grimes-sevdaliza-nothing-lasts-forever-single-1234869580/|title=Grimes Teams Up With Iranian-Dutch Artist Sevdaliza for 'Nothing Lasts Forever'|magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]|date=November 3, 2023|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231103102011/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/grimes-sevdaliza-nothing-lasts-forever-single-1234869580/|archive-date=November 3, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|first=Liberty|last=Dunworth|url=https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-teams-up-with-sevdaliza-on-ravey-new-song-nothing-lasts-forever-listen-3530066|title=Grimes teams up with Sevdaliza on ravey new song 'Nothing Lasts Forever'|magazine=[[NME]]|date=November 3, 2023|access-date=December 7, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231103131653/https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-teams-up-with-sevdaliza-on-ravey-new-song-nothing-lasts-forever-listen-3530066|archive-date=November 3, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> In December, it was announced that Grimes would be partnering with the toy Curio company to launch an interactive AI toy named "Grok" that she provided the voice for.<ref>{{cite web|first=Katie|last=Notopoulos|url=https://www.businessinsider.com/grimes-ai-toy-grok-not-related-elon-musk-grok-xai-2023-12|title=Grimes just launched an AI toy named 'Grok.' No, it's not related to Elon Musk's Grok.|work=[[Business Insider]]|date=December 14, 2023|access-date=December 17, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231215042641/https://www.businessinsider.com/grimes-ai-toy-grok-not-related-elon-musk-grok-xai-2023-12|archive-date=December 15, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Tom|last=Breihan|url=https://www.stereogum.com/2245663/grimes-unveils-grok-an-ai-childrens-toy-unrelated-to-elon-musks-grok/news/|title=Grimes Unveils Grok, An AI Children's Toy Unrelated To Elon Musk's Grok|work=[[Stereogum]]|date=December 14, 2023|access-date=December 17, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231215132948/https://www.stereogum.com/2245663/grimes-unveils-grok-an-ai-childrens-toy-unrelated-to-elon-musks-grok/news/|archive-date=December 15, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>

In April 2024, Grimes DJed at [[Coachella]] which was cut short due to technical problems.<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Halima|last=Jibril|url=https://www.dazeddigital.com/music/article/62393/1/grimes-coachella-performance-set-2024|title=Grimes apologises for 'worst performance in history of Coachella'|magazine=[[Dazed]]|date=April 15, 2024|access-date=October 12, 2024}}</ref> Grimes restarted songs several times, punctuated by loud yelps and screeches of frustration, telling the crowd she was experiencing speed issues with her tracks which were playing double their normal tempo and she was having trouble “doing the math”.<ref>{{cite web|first=Surej|last=Singh|url=https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-dj-set-at-coachella-mired-by-technical-difficulties-social-media-reacts-3617464|title=Grimes' DJ set at Coachella mired by technical difficulties, social media reacts|work=[[NME]]|date=April 14, 2024|access-date=October 12, 2024}}</ref> Grimes claimed the problems came from her having outsourced preparation work to third parties due to time constraints.<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Mitchell|last=Peters|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/grimes-coachella-2024-apology-technical-difficulties-1235656322/|title=Grimes Apologizes for 'Major Technical Difficulties' During Coachella 2024 Set|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|date=April 14, 2024|access-date=April 22, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240415014121/https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/grimes-coachella-2024-apology-technical-difficulties-1235656322/|archive-date=April 15, 2024|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|first=Bonnie|last=McLaren|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/newsbeat-68816031|title=Coachella: Grimes apologises for technical difficulties|work=[[BBC News]]|date=April 15, 2024|access-date=April 22, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240415103758/https://www.bbc.com/news/newsbeat-68816031|archive-date=April 15, 2024|url-status=live}}</ref> Media referred to it as the "worst performance in the history of Coachella".<ref>{{cite news|first=Farley|last=Elliott|url=https://www.sfgate.com/sf-culture/article/grimes-set-technical-difficulty-coachella-19402352.php|title='Worst performance in the history of Coachella': Tech issues doom star act|work=SF Gate|date=April 14, 2024|access-date=February 9, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240415151631/https://www.sfgate.com/sf-culture/article/grimes-set-technical-difficulty-coachella-19402352.php|archive-date=April 15, 2024|url-status=live}}</ref>

On September 20, 2024, Grimes released a remix of a song called "[[Supernova (Aespa song)|Supernova]]", originally by [[K-pop]] group [[Aespa]] as part of "iScreaM Vol.33 : Supernova / Armageddon Remixes", the 33rd EP in a series of K-pop remixes by [[SM Entertainment]] sub-label "[[ScreaM Records]]".<ref>{{cite news|first=Gladys|last=Yeo|url=https://www.nme.com/news/music/aespa-enlist-grimes-for-brand-new-remix-of-supernova-3795405|title=Aespa enlist Grimes for brand-new remix of 'Supernova's|work=[[NME]]|date=September 20, 2024|access-date=September 21, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240920064121/https://www.nme.com/news/music/aespa-enlist-grimes-for-brand-new-remix-of-supernova-3795405|archive-date=September 20, 2024|url-status=live}}</ref>

On October 29, 2024, Grimes released a remix of [[Magdalena Bay (duo)|Magdalena Bay]]'s "[[Image (song)|Image]]".<ref>{{cite web|first=Walden|last=Green|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-remixes-magdalena-bays-image-listen/|title=Grimes Remixes Magdalena Bay's "Image": Listen|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=October 29, 2024|access-date=March 3, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241107064142/https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-remixes-magdalena-bays-image-listen/|archive-date=November 7, 2024|url-status=live}}</ref> Magdalena Bay had previously credited Grimes as an inspiration for their work.<ref>{{cite web|first=Cat|last=Zhang|url=https://pitchfork.com/features/rising/magdalena-bay-mercurial-world-interview/|title=Magdalena Bay Are More Online Than You|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=July 20, 2021|access-date=February 25, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240403141551/https://pitchfork.com/features/rising/magdalena-bay-mercurial-world-interview/|archive-date=April 3, 2024|url-status=live}}</ref>

On February 24, 2025, two [[Demo (music)|demos]] had been uploaded to Grimes' [[SoundCloud]]: "The Fool" and "I Don't Give a Fuck, I'm Insane". The latter appeared on other streaming sites a few hours later.<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Gil|last=Kaufman|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/grimes-2-unreleased-demos-stop-posting-pics-son-1235909557/|title=Grimes Shares 2 Unreleased Demos, Says She Would Really Like 'People to Stop Posting Images of My Kid Everywhere'|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|date=February 25, 2025|access-date=March 3, 2025|archive-url=https://archive.today/20250225154759/https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/grimes-2-unreleased-demos-stop-posting-pics-son-1235909557/|archive-date=February 25, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> Grimes co-produced [[Adéla (singer)|Adéla]]'s song, "Machine Girl", which was released on February 28, 2025. Grimes also made a cameo in the song's music video alongside [[Sofia Wylie]].<ref>{{cite web|first=Damian|last=Jones|url=https://www.nme.com/news/grimes-produces-adelas-new-single-machine-girl-cameos-in-raunchy-video-3842350|title=Grimes produces Adéla's new single 'Machine Girl', cameos in raunchy video|work=[[NME]]|date=February 28, 2025|access-date=March 3, 2025|archive-url=https://archive.today/20250303222731/https://www.nme.com/news/grimes-produces-adelas-new-single-machine-girl-cameos-in-raunchy-video-3842350|archive-date=March 3, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> On October 17, 2025, Grimes released the single "Artificial Angels".<ref>{{cite web|first=Paolo|last=Ragusa|url=https://consequence.net/2025/10/grimes-artificial-angels-stream/|title=Grimes Reveals New Song “Artificial Angels” Written from the Perspective of AI: Stream|work=[[Consequence (publication)|Consequence]]|date=October 17, 2025|access-date=October 18, 2025|archive-url=https://archive.today/20251018182153/https://consequence.net/2025/10/grimes-artificial-angels-stream/|archive-date=October 18, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> A music video for the song was released on October 20.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.thecelebpost.com/video/71068-grimes-drops-bizarre-artificial-angels-mv|title=Grimes drops bizarre ‘Artificial Angels’ MV|work=The Celeb Post|date=October 21, 2025|access-date=October 21, 2025|archive-url=https://archive.today/20251021213622/https://www.thecelebpost.com/video/71068-grimes-drops-bizarre-artificial-angels-mv|archive-date=October 21, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref>

==Artistry==
===Musical style===
[[File:GrimesHardRockCafeMakati.jpg|thumb|Grimes at Hard Rock Café Makati in 2013]]
Grimes' music has been described with a number of labels, including [[synth-pop]], [[electropop]], [[art pop]], [[indie pop]], [[dream pop]], [[experimental pop]], [[dance-pop]], [[Pop music|pop]], [[Avant-pop|avant-garde pop]], [[Lo-fi music|lo-fi]], [[Dance music|dance]], [[Witch house (genre)|witch house]], [[Electronic music|electronic]], [[glo-fi]], [[bedroom pop]], and [[electronica]] with elements of [[Rock music|rock]], [[Hip hop music|hip hop]], [[Contemporary R&B|R&B]], [[Contemporary folk music|folk]], [[drum and bass]], and [[Classical music|classical]].{{refn|group=note|Musical styles:{{columns-list|colwidth=20em| 
*"synth-pop"<ref name="Blabbermouth Nihilist Blues"/><ref name="ny">{{cite web|first=Laura H.|last=Holson|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2012/03/08/fashion/claire-boucher-known-as-grimes-mines-beauty-from-the-dark-side.html|title=Claire Boucher, known as Grimes, Mines Beauty from the Dark Side|work=[[The New York Times]]|date=March 7, 2012|access-date=June 15, 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220429214157/https://www.nytimes.com/2012/03/08/fashion/claire-boucher-known-as-grimes-mines-beauty-from-the-dark-side.html|archive-date=April 29, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|first=Eric Renner|last=Brown|url=https://ew.com/article/2015/10/26/grimes-shares-album-release-date-new-music-and-surreal-video/|title=Grimes announces 'Art Angels' album with surreal new music video|magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]|date=October 26, 2015|access-date=December 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406032144/https://ew.com/article/2015/10/26/grimes-shares-album-release-date-new-music-and-surreal-video/|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|first=Matt|last=Moen|url=https://www.papermag.com/grimes-player-of-games-video-2656092632.html?rebelltitem=5|title=Grimes Has a Lightsaber|magazine=[[Paper (magazine)|Paper Mag]]|date=December 22, 2021|access-date=December 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022855/https://www.papermag.com/grimes-player-of-games-video-2656092632.html?rebelltitem=5|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|first=Sarah|last=Jamieson|url=https://diymag.com/archive/grimes-i-really-dont-like-the-quirky-tag|title=Grimes: 'I Really Don't Like The Quirky Tag'|magazine=[[DIY (magazine)|DIY]]|date=November 4, 2023|access-date=December 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220723052115/https://diymag.com/archive/grimes-i-really-dont-like-the-quirky-tag|archive-date=July 23, 2022|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Josiah|last=Hughes|url=https://exclaim.ca/music/article/grimes_gear_stolen_after_manchester_show|title=Grimes' Gear Stolen After Manchester Show|work=[[Exclaim!]]|date=August 31, 2012|access-date=December 11, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210806002429/https://exclaim.ca/music/article/grimes_gear_stolen_after_manchester_show|archive-date=August 6, 2021|url-status=live}}</ref>
