According to ''[[Vulture.com|Vulture]]'', "[Grimes moved away] from the creepy, lo-fi R&B of her early releases to the futuristic [[dance-pop]] of her...[third] album, ''[[Visions (Grimes album)|Visions]]''."<ref name="aphex" /> For her fourth studio, ''[[Art Angels]]'', Grimes learned how to play guitar and violin.<ref name="Brian Hiatt"/> She stated "I didn't want to play the keys, 'cause I don't want to be considered synth-pop."<ref name="Brian Hiatt"/> ''[[Rolling Stone]]'' described the album as a move away from her "hazy synth-pop toward an off-kilter guitars-and-beats sound", and "uses rock sounds in a really different context".<ref name="Brian Hiatt"/> Grimes described her fifth studio album ''[[Miss Anthropocene]]'' as "mostly ethereal [[nu metal]]".<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Salvatore|last=Maicki|url=https://www.thefader.com/2019/03/20/grimes-new-album-2019-miss-anthrop0cene-announcement|title=Grimes details "nu-metal" fifth album Miss_Anthrop0cene|magazine=[[The Fader]]|date=March 20, 2019|access-date=December 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230404101205/https://www.thefader.com/2019/03/20/grimes-new-album-2019-miss-anthrop0cene-announcement|archive-date=April 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> ''[[The Guardian]]'' summarised her musical style: "By sounding a little like everything you've ever heard, the whole sounds like nothing you've ever heard."<ref name="one">{{cite web|first=Hermione|last=Hoby|url=https://www.theguardian.com/music/2012/jan/29/grimes-boucher-one-to-watch|title=One to watch: Grimes|work=[[The Guardian]]|date=January 28, 2012|access-date=June 15, 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140104052140/http://www.theguardian.com/music/2012/jan/29/grimes-boucher-one-to-watch|archive-date=January 4, 2014|url-status=live}}</ref> ''[[The Japan Times]]'' wrote that Grimes' "otherworldly, [[Ableton]]-assisted music is crammed full of hooks fit to sit alongside [[Rihanna]] and [[Taylor Swift]] in the [[Top 40]]".<ref name="Lindsay">{{cite web|first=Cam|last=Lindsay|url=https://www.japantimes.co.jp/culture/2016/01/21/music/grimes-set-challenge-definition-pop/|title=Grimes is set to challenge your definition of pop|work=[[The Japan Times]]|date=January 21, 2016|access-date=November 22, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171201042842/https://www.japantimes.co.jp/culture/2016/01/21/music/grimes-set-challenge-definition-pop/|archive-date=December 1, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref> ''[[Dazed]]'' stated: "In a sense, she'd always thrived on being too pop for indie and too indie for pop".<ref>{{cite web|first=Owen|last=Myers|url=http://www.dazeddigital.com/music/article/26282/1/grimes-weird-science|title=Grimes: Weird Science|work=[[Dazed]]|date=September 15, 2015|access-date=November 22, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171116021822/http://www.dazeddigital.com/music/article/26282/1/grimes-weird-science|archive-date=November 16, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref> Her lyrics were described by ''The Guardian'' as "generally elusive and impressionistic, shying away from specifics".<ref name="nine"/> Grimes is a [[soprano]].<ref>{{cite web|first=Abby|last=Jonhston|url=http://www.austinchronicle.com/daily/music/2012-03-01/grimes-circumambient/|title=Grimes: Circumambient|work=[[The Austin Chronicle]]|date=March 1, 2012|access-date=March 17, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180723123020/https://www.austinchronicle.com/daily/music/2012-03-01/grimes-circumambient/|archive-date=July 23, 2018|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Robert|last=Christgau|url=https://www.robertchristgau.com/get_artist.php?name=Grimes|title=Grimes: Art Angels Review|work=[[Robert Christgau]]|date=2015|access-date=March 17, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210235141/https://www.robertchristgau.com/get_artist.php?name=Grimes|archive-date=February 10, 2018|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Amy|last=Pettifer|url=http://thequietus.com/articles/19212-grimes-art-angels-review|title=Grimes: Art Angels Review|work=[[The Quietus]]|date=November 12, 2015|access-date=March 17, 2018}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Heather|last=Phares|url=https://www.allmusic.com/album/visions-mw0002289255|title=Visions – Grimes|work=[[AllMusic]]|access-date=March 17, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180317165017/https://www.allmusic.com/album/visions-mw0002289255|archive-date=March 17, 2018|url-status=live}}</ref> ''[[The Daily Telegraph]]'' described her vocals as "sweet, thin and hazy".<ref>{{cite web|first=Helen|last=Brown|url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/music/what-to-listen-to/grimes-art-angels-album-review-weird-and-wonderful/|title=Grimes: Art Angels, album review: 'weird and wonderful'|work=[[The Daily Telegraph]]|date=November 24, 2015|access-date=December 5, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151209161625/http://www.telegraph.co.uk/music/what-to-listen-to/grimes-art-angels-album-review-weird-and-wonderful/|archive-date=December 9, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref> She utilizes [[loop (music)|looping]] and layering techniques, particularly with vocals; many of her songs feature layers of over fifty different vocal tracks which create an "ethereal" sound.<ref name="ny"/> Her lyrical themes include [[science fiction]], [[feminism]], and [[climate change]].<ref name="bio-allmusic1"/> Her fifth studio album ''Miss Anthropocene'' has been considered to be a loose [[concept album]] about an "[[Anthropomorphism|anthropomorphic]] goddess of climate change" inspired by [[Roman mythology]]<ref>{{cite web|first=Will|last=Richards|url=https://www.nme.com/blogs/nme-blogs/grimes-new-album-miss_anthropocene-release-date-tracklist-everything-know-far-2531642|title=Grimes' new album 'Miss_Anthropocene': release date, tracklist and everything we know so far|work=[[NME]]|date=August 13, 2019|access-date=December 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022855/https://www.nme.com/blogs/nme-blogs/grimes-new-album-miss_anthropocene-release-date-tracklist-everything-know-far-2531642|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> and [[villain]]y.<ref name=":0">{{cite magazine|first=Kevin EG|last=Perry|url=https://crackmagazine.net/article/long-reads/grimes-is-ready-to-play-the-villain/|title=Cover Story: Grimes is ready to play the villain|magazine=[[Crack (magazine)|Crack]]|date=April 16, 2019|access-date=December 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230603170859/https://crackmagazine.net/article/long-reads/grimes-is-ready-to-play-the-villain/|archive-date=June 3, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> Heather Phares of [[AllMusic]] described the album as a "brooding embodiment of climate change".<ref name="bio-allmusic1"/> In the single "So Heavy I Fell Through the Earth" she also experimented with AI-generated music using the [[NSynth]] neural synthesizer.<ref name=":0"/>

Grimes described her music as "[[Attention deficit disorder|ADD]] music", shifting frequently and dramatically – "I go through phases a lot."<ref>{{Cite journal|last1=Zhong|first1=Fan|date=June 2012|title=On the Verge: Grimes|journal=[[W (magazine)|W]]|volume=41|issue=6|page=35|url=http://www.wmagazine.com/celebrities/2012/06/grimes-claire-boucher-musician-visions|access-date=June 9, 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130609122719/http://www.wmagazine.com/celebrities/2012/06/grimes-claire-boucher-musician-visions|archive-date=June 9, 2013|url-status=dead}}</ref> She said "Most music with traditional verse, chorus and bridge structures can probably be considered 'pop'. But I think most people think about Top 40 these days when they use the word 'pop', and I'm emphatically not from that world."<ref name="Lindsay"/> She said that [[Panda Bear (musician)|Panda Bear]]'s 2007 album ''[[Person Pitch]]'' "jumpstarted" her mind. She explains, "Up until that point I had basically only made weird atonal [[drone music]], with no sense of songwriting. I barely understood anything about music ... But suddenly all music clicked into place and seemed so simple and easy. I was pretty much able to spontaneously write songs immediately after listening to this album once."<ref name="stereogum.com">{{cite web|first=Peter|last=Helman|url=https://www.stereogum.com/1857227/grimes-writes-about-5-albums-that-changed-her-life/news/|title=Grimes Writes About 5 Albums That Changed Her Life|work=[[Stereogum]]|date=February 3, 2016|access-date=July 19, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160423223454/http://www.stereogum.com/1857227/grimes-writes-about-5-albums-that-changed-her-life/news/|archive-date=April 23, 2016|url-status=live}}</ref>

===Influences===
Her work has been likened to various artists, including [[Björk]],<ref name="nine"/> [[Julianna Barwick]],<ref name="caramanica1">{{cite web|first=Jon|last=Caramanica|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/21/arts/music/reviews-of-albums-from-grimes-galactic-and-tyga.html|title=Reviews of Albums From Grimes, Galactic and Tyga|work=[[The New York Times]]|date=February 20, 2012|access-date=February 21, 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120816143133/http://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/21/arts/music/reviews-of-albums-from-grimes-galactic-and-tyga.html|archive-date=August 16, 2012|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Siouxsie Sioux]],<ref name="caramanica1"/> and [[Enya]].<ref name="ny"/> She has stated that she loves British rock bands like [[Bring Me the Horizon]] and [[Foals (band)|Foals]].<ref name="Brian Hiatt"/> She was described by ''Tastemakers Magazine'' as an "alien love-child of [[Aphex Twin]] and [[ABBA]]".<ref name="taste">{{cite magazine|first=Leslie|last=Fowle|url=http://tastemakersmag.com/reviews/cd-reviews/2012/grimes-visions/|title=Grimes – Visions|magazine=Tastemakers Mag|date=March 14, 2012|access-date=June 14, 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120428211101/http://tastemakersmag.com/reviews/cd-reviews/2012/grimes-visions/|archive-date=April 28, 2012|url-status=dead}}</ref> While making her third studio album, Grimes was listening to [[Aphex Twin]], [[Black Dice]], [[Dungeon Family]], [[Michael Jackson]], [[New Edition]], [[Outkast]], [[Nine Inch Nails]], [[Burial (musician)|Burial]], [[TLC (group)|TLC]], [[Mariah Carey]] and stated "I'm into the really caustic beats, the kind of sharp drum and bass kind of stuff. Really nice vocals too, with lots of tight harmonies at the same time."<ref name="aphex" />

Grimes cites [[Blink-182]] as an influence in her [[Amoeba Music|Amoeba Records]] "What's In My Bag?" episode where she picked one of their live DVDs.<ref name="blink182">{{cite web|first=Maria|last=Sherman|url=https://www.villagevoice.com/2013/09/11/i-was-in-an-all-girl-blink-182-cover-band-called-dumpweed/|title=I Was in an All-Girl Blink-182 Cover Band Called Dumpweed|work=[[The Village Voice]]|date=September 11, 2013|access-date=September 12, 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130913095543/http://blogs.villagevoice.com/music/2013/09/blink_182_most_important_90s_band.php|archive-date=September 13, 2013|url-status=dead}}</ref> Grimes considers [[Blue Hawaii (band)|Blue Hawaii]] "a big part of [her] family in Montreal".<ref name="fallon">{{cite web|first=Patric|last=Fallon|url=https://www.xlr8r.com/features/2012/02/high-five-grimes/|title=High Five: Grimes|date=February 1, 2012|access-date=June 17, 2012|work=[[XLR8R]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160915075653/https://www.xlr8r.com/features/2012/02/high-five-grimes/|archive-date=September 15, 2016|url-status=live}}</ref> Grimes stated that [[Cocteau Twins]]<ref name="straightu">{{cite web|first=John|last=Lucas|url=https://www.straight.com/article-607216/vancouver/grimes-taps-eclectic-set-influences|title=Grimes taps into eclectic set of influences|work=[[The Georgia Straight]]|date=February 16, 2012|access-date=June 17, 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150211044456/http://www.straight.com/article-607216/vancouver/grimes-taps-eclectic-set-influences|archive-date=February 11, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref> are "one of the first bands I was into that was considered [[Alternative music|alternative]]". In a tweet, Grimes replied to someone saying that her recent influences were [[Chris Isaak]], [[St. Vincent (musician)|St. Vincent]], and [[Mindless Self Indulgence]].<ref name="bowie">{{cite web|first=David|last=Renshaw|url=https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-49-1212018|title=Grimes finishes work on new 'glam rock' song inspired by David Bowie and Queen|work=[[NME]]|date=December 12, 2014|access-date=September 7, 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170305200845/http://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-49-1212018|archive-date=March 5, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref> The theories of her second studio album, ''[[Halfaxa]]'' were inspired by [[Hildegard of Bingen]].<ref>{{cite web|first=Quinn|last=Moreland|url=https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/21775-halfaxa/|title=Halfaxa Grimes|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=April 6, 2016|access-date=December 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160408203100/https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/21775-halfaxa/|archive-date=April 8, 2016|url-status=live}}</ref>

Before releasing her fourth studio album, ''[[Art Angels]]'', Grimes described one of her upcoming songs as a [[glam rock]] track inspired by [[David Bowie]] and [[Queen (band)|Queen]].<ref name="bowie"/> ''Art Angels'' was also influenced by [[Billy Joel]], [[Bruce Springsteen]], and [[The Godfather (film series)|''The Godfather'']] movies.<ref name="bruce">{{cite web|first=Alex|last=Young|url=https://consequence.net/2015/10/grimes-new-album-is-called-art-angels-features-a-song-about-al-pacino-as-transgender-vampire/|title=Grimes' new album is called Art Angels, features a song about Al Pacino as transgender vampire|work=[[Consequence (publication)|Consequence]]|date=October 19, 2015|access-date=September 7, 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160905074253/http://consequenceofsound.net/2015/10/grimes-new-album-is-called-art-angels-features-a-song-about-al-pacino-as-transgender-vampire/|archive-date=September 5, 2016|url-status=live}}</ref> Grimes said that while touring with [[How to Dress Well]], his song "Suicide Dream 2" "made me tear up every night... [and] after this tour I got really re-inspired, went home, and immediately wrote [songs that] are, in my opinion, the best shit I've ever done."<ref name="fallon"/> Early on, Grimes stated that "an early diet of the [[Spice Girls]], [[Marilyn Manson (band)|Marilyn Manson]], OutKast and [[Skinny Puppy]] drove her to build pop songs out of the harsher sonic textures she rarely heard on the radio."<ref name="Richards">{{cite news|first=Chris|last=Richards|url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/entertainment/music/no-room-for-grimes-in-a-genre-box/2012/09/06/3335160a-f1ed-11e1-adc6-87dfa8eff430_story.html|title=No Room for Grimes in a Genre Box|newspaper=[[The Washington Post]]|date=September 6, 2012|access-date=November 26, 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120912090534/https://www.washingtonpost.com/entertainment/music/no-room-for-grimes-in-a-genre-box/2012/09/06/3335160a-f1ed-11e1-adc6-87dfa8eff430_story.html|archive-date=September 12, 2012|url-status=dead}}</ref> Some of her other influences include [[Jedi Mind Tricks]],<ref name="jmt">{{cite web|first=Cam|last=Lindsay|url=http://exclaim.ca/music/article/grimes_talks_her_visions|title=Grimes Talks Her 'Visions'|work=[[Exclaim!]]|date=February 13, 2012|access-date= September 6, 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160610143909/http://exclaim.ca/music/article/grimes_talks_her_visions|archive-date=June 10, 2016|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Kenji Kawai]],<ref name="japan">{{cite web|first=Jason|last=Richards|url=http://www.japantimes.co.jp/culture/2013/03/21/music/japans-influence-on-grimes-grows-deeper/|title=Japan's influence on Grimes grows deeper|work=[[The Japan Times]]|date=March 21, 2013|access-date=January 1, 2016|language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151226002933/http://www.japantimes.co.jp/culture/2013/03/21/music/japans-influence-on-grimes-grows-deeper/|archive-date=December 26, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Yoko Kanno]],<ref name="japan"/> [[Alicia Keys]],<ref name="Zoladz">{{cite web|first=Lindsay|last=Zoladz|url=https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/15439-darkbloom-ep/|title=Album Reviews: d'Eon / Grimes: Darkbloom EP|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=May 19, 2011|access-date=June 7, 2011|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110522111113/http://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/15439-darkbloom-ep/|archive-date=May 22, 2011|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Christina Aguilera]],<ref>{{cite news|first=Kat|last=Stoeffel|url=https://observer.com/2012/03/snip-snip-bang-bang-from-rooney-to-runway-cropped-tops-come-to-the-forehead/|title=Snip, Snip, Bangs, Bangs! From Rooney to Runway, Cropped Tops Come to the Fore(head)|newspaper=[[The Observer]]|date=March 14, 2012|access-date=September 3, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230404140002/https://observer.com/2012/03/snip-snip-bang-bang-from-rooney-to-runway-cropped-tops-come-to-the-forehead/|archive-date=April 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Panda Bear (musician)|Panda Bear]],<ref name="Sanneh"/><ref name="Zoladz"/> [[Bikini Kill]],<ref name="Sanneh"/> [[Kate Bush]],<ref>{{cite web|first=Elise|last=Soutar|url=https://www.pastemagazine.com/music/kate-bush/stranger-things-season-4/|title=A Beginner's Guide to Kate Bush for Stranger Things Fans|work=[[Paste (magazine)|Paste]]|date=June 1, 2022|access-date=July 20, 2022|archive-date=July 20, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220720172454/https://www.pastemagazine.com/music/kate-bush/stranger-things-season-4/|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Al Green]],<ref name="Zoladz"/><ref name="algreen">{{cite web|first=Stephen|last=Kerr|url=http://www.dummymag.com/new-music/grimes-interview-so-many-worlds|title=Grimes interview: "So many worlds."|work=Dummy Mag|date=August 21, 2010|access-date=October 6, 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161207072418/http://www.dummymag.com/new-music/grimes-interview-so-many-worlds|archive-date=December 7, 2016|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Salem (Michigan band)|Salem]],<ref name="Zoladz"/> [[Trent Reznor]],<ref>{{cite web|first=Chandler|last=Levack|url=https://www.cbc.ca/arts/grimes-went-from-industry-shaking-genius-to-punchline-in-a-decade-are-we-treating-her-fairly-1.5470717|title=Grimes went from industry-shaking genius to punchline in a decade. Are we treating her fairly?|work=[[Canadian Broadcasting Corporation|CBC]]|date=February 24, 2020|access-date=December 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230901022510/https://www.cbc.ca/arts/grimes-went-from-industry-shaking-genius-to-punchline-in-a-decade-are-we-treating-her-fairly-1.5470717|archive-date=September 1, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Peter|last=Helman|url=https://www.stereogum.com/1819707/grimes-teases-happy-and-angry-album-full-of-diss-tracks-guitar/news/|title=Grimes Teases "Happy And Angry" Album Full Of Diss Tracks, Guitar|work=[[Stereogum]]|date=July 28, 2015|access-date=December 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022855/https://www.stereogum.com/1819707/grimes-teases-happy-and-angry-album-full-of-diss-tracks-guitar/news/|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Tool (band)|Tool]],<ref name="stereogum.com"/> [[Yeah Yeah Yeahs]],<ref name="stereogum.com"/> [[Beyoncé]],<ref>{{cite web|first=Peter|last=Helman|url=https://www.stereogum.com/1857227/grimes-writes-about-5-albums-that-changed-her-life/news/|title=Grimes Writes About 5 Albums That Changed Her Life|work=[[Stereogum]]|date=February 3, 2016|access-date=January 26, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230307060105/https://www.stereogum.com/1857227/grimes-writes-about-5-albums-that-changed-her-life/news/|archive-date=March 7, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> and [[Paramore]].<ref name="paramore">{{cite magazine|first=Nicole|last=Pajer|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/grimes-shares-details-of-experimental-next-album-1558809/|title=Grimes Offers Precise Update on 'Experimental' Next Album|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|date=April 18, 2013|access-date=September 8, 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161008201526/http://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/pop-shop/1558809/grimes-shares-details-of-experimental-next-album|archive-date=October 8, 2016|url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Visual art ===
Grimes designs her [[album cover|album art]] for all of her albums, gig fliers, comic book covers,<ref name="NME Cover art">{{cite web|first=Emily|last=Barker|url=https://www.nme.com/photos/write-the-songs-draw-the-cover-when-artists-make-their-own-album-sleeves-1408928|title=Write The Songs, Draw The Cover – When Artists Make Their Own Album Sleeves|work=[[NME]]|date=November 3, 2015|access-date=December 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406032916/https://www.nme.com/photos/write-the-songs-draw-the-cover-when-artists-make-their-own-album-sleeves-1408928|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> and merchandise.<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Jordan|last=Darville|url=https://www.thefader.com/2018/11/26/grimes-new-music-release-date-opens-merch-shop|title=Grimes announces new music release date, opens merch shop|magazine=[[The Fader]]|date=November 26, 2018|access-date=December 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022856/https://www.thefader.com/2018/11/26/grimes-new-music-release-date-opens-merch-shop|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> She has done exhibitions showcasing her works and has stated that "[she has] always been a visual artist".<ref name="NME Cover art"/> Her art is influenced by Japanese [[anime]], [[manga]], and [[comics|comic]] artists such as [[Charles Burns (cartoonist)|Charles Burns]] and [[Daniel Clowes]].<ref name="abcnews.go.com">{{cite web|first=Mimi|last=Wong|url=https://abcnews.go.com/blogs/entertainment/2012/12/grimes-artistic-genesis-experimental-electronic-musician-flirts-with-pop/|title=Grimes' Artistic 'Genesis': Experimental Electronic Musician Flirts With Pop|work=[[ABC News (United States)|ABC News]]|date=December 6, 2012|access-date=December 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022855/https://abcnews.go.com/blogs/entertainment/2012/12/grimes-artistic-genesis-experimental-electronic-musician-flirts-with-pop/|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> Her illustrations have appeared in gallery shows, including at [[Guggenheim Museum Bilbao]].<ref>{{cite web|first=Elisabetta|last=Rastelli|url=https://www.kooness.com/posts/magazine/grimess-first-online-exhibition|title=When a Musician double lives as a visual artist...|work=Kooness|date=June 9, 2020|access-date=December 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406024400/https://www.kooness.com/posts/magazine/grimess-first-online-exhibition|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> She created an alternate cover for [[Image Comics]]' ''[[The Wicked + The Divine]]'',<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.factmag.com/2015/07/12/grimes-design-wicked-divine-comic-cover/|title=Grimes has designed an amazing comic book cover|magazine=[[Fact (UK magazine)|Factmag]]|date=July 12, 2015|access-date=December 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022855/https://www.factmag.com/2015/07/12/grimes-design-wicked-divine-comic-cover/|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|author=Luke Morgan Britton|url=https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-39-1217357|title=Grimes designs cover art for new comic book|work=[[NME]]|date=July 12, 2015|access-date=December 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022858/https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-39-1217357|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Alex|last=Siber|url=https://www.complex.com/pigeons-and-planes/2015/07/grimes-designs-comic-book-cover-art|title=Grimes Flexes Graphic Talent with Comic Book Cover Art|work=Complex|date=July 12, 2015|access-date=December 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022858/https://www.complex.com/pigeons-and-planes/2015/07/grimes-designs-comic-book-cover-art|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> and designed a capsule collection of t-shirts for [[Hedi Slimane]]'s Saint Laurent, in 2013.<ref>{{cite web|author=deitchm|url=https://www.mtv.com/news/i57k93/grimes-collaborates-with-hedi-slimane-on-saint-laurent-capsule-collection|title=Grimes Collaborates With Hedi Slimane On Saint Laurent Capsule Collection|work=[[MTV News]]|date=February 26, 2013|access-date=December 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406024357/https://www.mtv.com/news/i57k93/grimes-collaborates-with-hedi-slimane-on-saint-laurent-capsule-collection|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Teofilo|last=Killip|url=https://www.complex.com/style/2013/02/saint-laurent-paris-taps-grimes-for-a-5-piece-capsule-collection|title=Saint Laurent Paris Taps Grimes for a Five Piece Capsule Collection|work=Complex|date=February 28, 2013|access-date=December 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022855/https://www.complex.com/style/2013/02/saint-laurent-paris-taps-grimes-for-a-5-piece-capsule-collection|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> That year, she also curated a two-day event at the Audio Visual Arts Gallery in New York City with a silent auction to benefit the Native Women's Association of Canada's campaign to raise awareness of violence against aboriginal women in Canada.<ref>{{cite web|first=Tyler|last=McCall|url=http://fashionista.com/2013/02/grimes-designs-capsule-collection-of-t-shirts-for-saint-laurent-paris|title=Grimes Designs Capsule Collection of T-Shirts for Saint Laurent Paris|work=[[Fashionista (website)|Fashionista]]|date=February 26, 2013|access-date=July 31, 2022|archive-date=May 25, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240525024529/https://fashionista.com/2013/02/grimes-designs-capsule-collection-of-t-shirts-for-saint-laurent-paris|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Jenn|last=Pelly|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/45692-grimes-claire-boucher-to-stage-art-show-in-nyc/|title=Grimes' Claire Boucher to Stage Art Show in NYC|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=March 8, 2012|access-date=March 8, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170309065138/http://pitchfork.com/news/45692-grimes-claire-boucher-to-stage-art-show-in-nyc/|archive-date=March 9, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref> In early 2021, she sold original digital art in the form of [[non-fungible token]]s for $5.8 million.<ref>{{cite web|first=Grace|last=Kay|url=https://www.businessinsider.com/grimes-nft-art-warnymph-sells-for-millions-20-minutes-2021-3|title=Grimes made $5.8 million in under 20 minutes selling crypto-based artwork|work=[[Insider Inc.|Business Insider]]|date=March 1, 2021|access-date=December 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022856/https://www.businessinsider.com/grimes-nft-art-warnymph-sells-for-millions-20-minutes-2021-3|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|first=Emily|last=Kirkpatrick|url=https://www.vanityfair.com/style/2021/03/grimes-art-sold-nft-cryptocurrency-auction-elon-musk-warnymph|title=Grimes's Digital Art of Spear-Wielding Babies Sells for $5.8 Million|magazine=[[Vanity Fair (magazine)|Vanity Fair]]|date=March 2, 2021|access-date=December 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230201233738/https://www.vanityfair.com/style/2021/03/grimes-art-sold-nft-cryptocurrency-auction-elon-musk-warnymph|archive-date=February 1, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> In May 2022, she said on Twitter she was joining the board of [[Unicorn DAO]], "to help their mission to fund/ develop female and non-binary lead [<nowiki/>''[[sic]]''] art and projects".
<ref>{{cite tweet|url=https://twitter.com/Grimezsz/status/1525981460561137664|author=Claire Elise Boucher|user=Grimezsz |number=1525981460561137664 |title=Donating my video 4 'New Gods' to @unicorndao_xxx to help their mission to fund develop female and non-binary lead art and projects 🤍 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220822221028/https://twitter.com/Grimezsz/status/1525981460561137664 |archive-date=2022-08-22}}</ref>
<ref>{{cite web|first=Kari|last=McMahon|url=https://www.businessinsider.com/pitch-deck-slide-unicorndao-pussy-riot-sia-grimes-beeple-crypto-2022-5|title=Pussy Riot-led UnicornDAO raised $4.5 million to support women and LGBTQ+ artists. Here's an exclusive look at the 8-slide pitch deck that helped onboard members like Yuga Labs, Beeple, Sia and Grimes.|work=[[Insider Inc.|Business Insider]]|date=May 23, 2022|access-date=July 31, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220701202628/https://www.businessinsider.com/pitch-deck-slide-unicorndao-pussy-riot-sia-grimes-beeple-crypto-2022-5|archive-date=July 1, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref>

==Personal life==
Grimes's brother Mac Boucher has played a role in creating a number of her music videos including "Violence", "Go", "[[Realiti (Grimes song)|Realiti]]", and "Venus Fly", among others.<ref>{{cite web|first=Jeff|last=Benjamin|url=https://www.fuse.tv/videos/2015/12/grimes-fuse-first-interview-realiti|title=Grimes On "Realiti": It "Wasn't Supposed To Be A Music Video"|work=[[Fuse (TV channel)|Fuse]]|date=December 8, 2015|access-date=May 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180510050919/https://www.fuse.tv/videos/2015/12/grimes-fuse-first-interview-realiti|archive-date=May 10, 2018|url-status=live}}</ref> She and her stepbrother, who raps under the name [[Jay Worthy]], collaborated on the single "Christmas Song", released on the Rough Trade bonus disc of her ''[[Visions (Grimes album)|Visions]]'' album.<ref>{{cite web|first=Luke|last=Morgan Britton|url=https://www.thelineofbestfit.com/news/latest-news/grimes-to-release-two-re-issues-of-visions-113949|title=Grimes to release two re-issues of 'Visions'|work=[[The Line of Best Fit]]|date=December 3, 2012|access-date=December 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022855/https://www.thelineofbestfit.com/news/latest-news/grimes-to-release-two-re-issues-of-visions-113949|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Evan|last=Minsker|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/48786-grimes-announces-visions-bonus-discs/|title=Grimes Announces Visions Bonus Discs|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=December 1, 2012|access-date=December 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022857/https://pitchfork.com/news/48786-grimes-announces-visions-bonus-discs/|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>

In 2009, Grimes and a friend attempted to travel down the [[Mississippi River]] to [[New Orleans]] from [[Minneapolis]] in a [[houseboat]] they built.<ref>{{cite web|first=Lora|last=Pabst|url=http://www.startribune.com/this-boat-don-t-float/49134952/|title=This boat don't float|work=[[Star Tribune]]|date=June 26, 2009|access-date=January 24, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250116183541/http://www.startribune.com/this-boat-don-t-float/49134952/|archive-date=January 16, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> Following several mishaps, including engine trouble and encounters with law enforcement, the houseboat was impounded by the city of Minneapolis. Grimes claims that elements of the story were exaggerated in the newspapers that reported on it at the time.<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Emilie|last=Friedlander|url=http://www.thefader.com/2015/07/28/grimes-cover-story-interview|title=Grimes In Reality|magazine=[[The Fader]]|date=July 28, 2015|access-date=May 23, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180607211612/http://www.thefader.com/2015/07/28/grimes-cover-story-interview|archive-date=June 7, 2018|url-status=live}}</ref> The adventure has been turned into an animated video narrated by [[T Bone Burnett]].<ref>{{cite web|first=Braudie|last=Blais-Billie|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/watch-grimes-float-down-the-mississippi-river-in-new-animated-video/|title=Grimes' Crazy 2009 Houseboat Adventure Turned Into Animated Video|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=May 23, 2018|access-date=May 23, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180524151821/https://pitchfork.com/news/watch-grimes-float-down-the-mississippi-river-in-new-animated-video/|archive-date=May 24, 2018|url-status=live}}</ref>

Grimes has been open about her past drug use, revealing intense periods during the creation of her third album ''[[Visions (Grimes album)|Visions]]'' in 2012, during which she "blacked out the windows and did tons of [[amphetamine]] and stayed up for three weeks and didn't eat anything".<ref name="Altered Zone"/> In 2014, she wrote a blog post expressing her aversion to hard drugs.<ref name="avclub Wikipedia drugs">{{cite web|first=William|last=Hughes|url=https://www.avclub.com/stop-posting-stuff-about-drugs-to-grimes-wikipedia-pag-1798271294|title=Stop posting stuff about drugs to Grimes' Wikipedia page, please|work=[[The A.V. Club]]|date=August 18, 2014|access-date=December 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230930115311/https://www.avclub.com/stop-posting-stuff-about-drugs-to-grimes-wikipedia-pag-1798271294|archive-date=September 30, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="dazeddigital Wikipedia drugs">{{cite web|first=Thomas|last=Gorton|url=http://www.dazeddigital.com/music/article/21303/1/grimes-pens-anti-drugs-note-on-tumblr|title=Grimes pens anti-drugs note on Tumblr|work=[[Dazed & Confused (magazine)|Dazed & Confused]]|date=August 19, 2014|access-date=August 23, 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140821030306/http://www.dazeddigital.com/music/article/21303/1/grimes-pens-anti-drugs-note-on-tumblr|archive-date=August 21, 2014|url-status=live}}</ref>

Grimes embraces her distinctive [[lisp]]<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/articles/1DtVghvFzDkDt3FC7gsM0S3/5-celebs-you-probably-didnt-know-had-speech-problems|title=5 celebs you probably didn't know had speech problems|work=[[BBC]]|access-date=December 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022855/https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/articles/1DtVghvFzDkDt3FC7gsM0S3/5-celebs-you-probably-didnt-know-had-speech-problems|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="C other name">{{Cite web|first=Laura|last=Hudson|url=https://www.theverge.com/2018/5/19/17372526/grimes-c-boucher-name-change-elon-musk|title=Encouraged by Elon Musk, Grimes changed her name to the speed of light|work=[[The Verge]]|date=May 19, 2018|access-date=November 11, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180705233256/https://www.theverge.com/2018/5/19/17372526/grimes-c-boucher-name-change-elon-musk|archive-date=July 5, 2018|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="C other name2">{{cite magazine|first=Khalila|last=Douze|url=https://www.culturedmag.com/article/2019/04/04/grimes-claire-boucher-c|title=The artist formerly known as Grimes|magazine=Cultured|date=April 4, 2019|access-date=December 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230407064733/https://www.culturedmag.com/article/2019/04/04/grimes-claire-boucher-c|archive-date=April 7, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> and has expressed no desire for speech therapy to alter it.<ref name="Teen Vogue">{{cite web|first=Stella|last=McCartney|url=https://www.teenvogue.com/story/grimes-interview-teen-vogue-april-2016|title=Grimes Opens Up About Beyoncé and Body Hair in Our April Issue|work=[[Teen Vogue]]|date=March 10, 2016|access-date=September 27, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170928005349/https://www.teenvogue.com/story/grimes-interview-teen-vogue-april-2016|archive-date=September 28, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref> Grimes has said that she is [[Autism|autistic]], saying she was previously misdiagnosed with [[restless legs syndrome]] and [[schizoaffective disorder]]. She described personal motor-skill issues when {{nowrap|"[she]}} went to check [her] kids and performed worse than them on every test".<ref>{{cite web|first=Derrick|last=Rossignol|url=https://uproxx.com/indie/grimes-autism-diagnosis|title=Grimes Recently Learned She Is Autistic And Revealed How She Realized That Might Be The Case|work=[[Uproxx]]|date=August 22, 2023|access-date=December 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230822122107/https://uproxx.com/indie/grimes-autism-diagnosis/|archive-date=August 22, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>

Frequently identified as a feminist musician during her early career, Grimes expressed frustration with this in 2015 by stating that it "really genders [her]" in a way that she does not identify with, adding that she does not relate strongly to female gender identity. Earlier that year, she had posted on [[Twitter]]: "I vibe in a gender-neutral space so I'm kinda impartial to pronouns."<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Owen|last=Myers|url=https://www.dazeddigital.com/music/article/26282/1/grimes-weird-science|title=Grimes: Weird Science|magazine=[[Dazed]]|date=September 15, 2015|access-date=August 2, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230328183149/https://www.dazeddigital.com/music/article/26282/1/grimes-weird-science|archive-date=March 28, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="UproxxGender">{{cite web|first=Derrick|last=Rossignol|url=https://uproxx.com/indie/grimes-gender-female-ish/|title=Grimes Says Her Gender Is 'Female-ish'|work=[[Uproxx]]|date=December 29, 2021|access-date=August 2, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220622210704/https://uproxx.com/indie/grimes-gender-female-ish/|archive-date=June 22, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref> In 2018, she made another post on the platform stating that she is "personally put off by the word 'woman' at least as far as my self id" and, in 2021, she called herself "female-ish".<ref name="UproxxGender"/> In June 2023 she told an interviewer, "I kinda like the patriarchy," saying "a lot of good things came from it." She went on to clarify, "I think it's sort of oppressive and overly dominant, and if you don't include women in things they can easily become toxic, you know."<ref>{{cite web|first=Joe|last=Harker|url=https://www.unilad.com/celebrity/grimes-likes-patriarchy-reporter-react-054336-20230617|title=Reporter doesn’t know how to react as Grimes admits she ‘likes the patriarchy’|work=[[UNILAD|Unilad]]|date=June 17, 2023|access-date=August 4, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230621053042/https://www.unilad.com/celebrity/grimes-likes-patriarchy-reporter-react-054336-20230617|archive-date=June 21, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>

In 2023, after members of the r/grimezs [[subreddit]] documented her affiliations with [[far-right]] figures, Grimes responded, "I'm called a Nazi because I happily am proud of white culture." She added that she wished to "emphasize the incredible accomplishments of others ... whilst allowing pride for white ppl accomplishments as well".<ref>{{cite web|first=Scoop|last=Harrison|url=https://consequence.net/2023/12/grimes-white-culture|title=Grimes: "I Happily Am Proud of White Culture"|work=[[Consequence (publication)|Consequence]]|date=December 31, 2023|access-date=January 1, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240101054802/https://consequence.net/2023/12/grimes-white-culture/|archive-date=January 1, 2024|url-status=live}}</ref> She also stated, "Every day I think fondly of the brown king [[Cyrus the Great]]".<ref>{{cite web|first=Dunworth|last=Liberty|url=https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-responds-to-critics-labelling-her-a-nazi-i-am-happily-proud-of-white-culture-what-if-humans-just-love-each-other-3564495|title=Grimes responds to critics labelling her a 'Nazi': 'I am happily proud of white culture – what if humans just love each other?'|work=[[NME]]|date=January 2, 2024|access-date=January 17, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240102121708/https://www.nme.com/news/music/grimes-responds-to-critics-labelling-her-a-nazi-i-am-happily-proud-of-white-culture-what-if-humans-just-love-each-other-3564495|archive-date=January 2, 2024|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Jibril">{{cite magazine|first=Halima|last=Jibril|url=https://www.dazeddigital.com/music/article/61674/1/grimes-says-she-is-proud-of-white-culture|title=Grimes says she is 'proud of white culture'|magazine=[[Dazed]]|date=January 2, 2024|access-date=February 6, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240102175225/https://www.dazeddigital.com/music/article/61674/1/grimes-says-she-is-proud-of-white-culture|archive-date=January 2, 2024|url-status=live}}</ref> The statement attracted widespread media criticism, with Halima Jibril writing for ''[[Dazed]]'' that Grimes was using "the same tiresome rhetoric white people have used for centuries while they oppress people of colour, reminding her critics that we should 'love each other'".<ref name="Jibril"/> She later attended far-right blogger [[Curtis Yarvin]]'s wedding.<ref>{{cite web|first=Julia|last=Black|url=https://www.theinformation.com/articles/the-far-right-guru-who-has-befriended-silicon-valleys-extreme-factions|title=The Far-Right Guru Who Has Befriended Silicon Valley's Extreme Factions|work=[[The Information (website)|The Information]]|date=August 9, 2024|access-date=October 12, 2024}}</ref> In January 2025, Grimes attended a party in [[Washington, D.C.]], alongside Yarvin, to celebrate the [[second inauguration of Donald Trump]].<ref>{{cite news|last=Voght|first=Kara|date=January 31, 2025|title=Butterworth's, MAGA's new hangout, is for the 'weirdos and freaks'|url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/style/power/2025/01/30/butterworths-capitol-hill-maga-hangout-trump/|newspaper=The Washington Post| access-date=February 7, 2025|archive-date=February 2, 2025|archive-url=https://archive.today/20250202113148/https://www.washingtonpost.com/style/power/2025/01/30/butterworths-capitol-hill-maga-hangout-trump/|url-status=live}}</ref>

Grimes has been accused of abusing [[non-disclosure agreement]]s (NDAs) and "bullying". In 2018, fellow singer [[Poppy (singer)|Poppy]] stated that she "got to watch her bully songwriters into signing NDA[s]". Poppy's former creative director [[Titanic Sinclair]] posted a screenshot to [[Instagram]] in 2023 with a caption saying, "I think bullying your ghostwriters into NDAs and never paying them is wrong".<ref>{{cite web|first=Anagricel|last=Duran|url=https://www.nme.com/news/music/poppys-former-creative-director-backs-claims-grimes-bullied-singer-into-signing-nda-3480482|title=Poppy's former creative director backs claims Grimes "bullied" singer into signing NDA|work=[[NME]]|date=August 9, 2023|access-date=March 30, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230810081557/https://www.nme.com/news/music/poppys-former-creative-director-backs-claims-grimes-bullied-singer-into-signing-nda-3480482|archive-date=August 10, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>

===Relationships===
From 2007 to 2010, Grimes was in an on-and-off relationship with [[Devon Welsh]], then lead vocalist of [[Majical Cloudz]].<ref name="PitchforkCloudz">{{cite web|first=Jenn|last=Pelly|url=https://pitchfork.com/features/cover-story/reader/majical-cloudz/|title=Fall Down Laughing: The Story of Majical Cloudz|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=June 25, 2015|access-date=December 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022900/https://pitchfork.com/features/cover-story/reader/majical-cloudz/|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> The two met in 2007 at a first-year dorm party while studying at McGill University.<ref name="PitchforkCloudz"/> From 2012 to 2018, Grimes was in a relationship with electronic musician [[Jaime Brooks]],<ref name="ExclaimGenders">{{cite web|first=Ian|last=Gormely|url=https://exclaim.ca/music/article/default_genders_escaped_the_spotlights_glare_to_make_main_pop_girl_2019_his_best_work_yet|title=Default Genders Escaped the Spotlight's Glare to Make 'Main Pop Girl 2019,' His Best Work Yet|work=[[Exclaim!]]|date=February 28, 2019|access-date=December 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022908/https://exclaim.ca/music/article/default_genders_escaped_the_spotlights_glare_to_make_main_pop_girl_2019_his_best_work_yet|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> who supported her on the Visions Tour performing as Elite Gymnastics.<ref name="MinnDailyTour">{{cite web|author=Tony|url=https://mndaily.com/212703/uncategorized/grimes-annouces-tour-local-duo-elite-gymnastics/|title=Grimes Announces Tour with Local Duo Elite Gymnastics|work=[[The Minnesota Daily]]|date=June 8, 2012|access-date=December 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022856/https://mndaily.com/212703/uncategorized/grimes-annouces-tour-local-duo-elite-gymnastics/|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="SpinBrooks">{{cite magazine|first=Marc|last=Hogan|url=https://www.spin.com/2013/08/default-genders-james-brooks-on-fraternity-controversy-response/|title=Default Genders' James Brooks: 'I Totally Failed'|magazine=[[Spin (magazine)|Spin]]|date=August 7, 2013|access-date=December 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406022855/https://www.spin.com/2013/08/default-genders-james-brooks-on-fraternity-controversy-response/|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>

In 2018, Grimes began a relationship with business magnate [[Elon Musk]].<ref name="CNBC_MuskSuit">{{cite news|first=Sara|last=Salinas|url=https://www.cnbc.com/2019/01/04/elon-musk-wants-grimes-out-of-a-lawsuit-over-tesla-take-private-tweet.html|title=Elon Musk wants Grimes out of a lawsuit over Tesla take-private tweet|work=[[CNBC]]|date=January 4, 2019|access-date=December 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230406024358/https://www.cnbc.com/2019/01/04/elon-musk-wants-grimes-out-of-a-lawsuit-over-tesla-take-private-tweet.html|archive-date=April 6, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> They met after discovering on Twitter that they had both independently made the same pun, relating to [[Rococo]] and the thought experiment [[Roko's basilisk]].<ref name="VoxWhoGrimes">{{cite web|first=Constance|last=Grady|url=https://www.vox.com/2018/8/16/17692700/azealia-banks-elon-musk-grimes-explained|title=The billionaire house hostage saga of Azealia Banks, Elon Musk, and Grimes, explained|work=[[Vox (website)|Vox]]|date=August 16, 2018|access-date=December 21, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181111091522/https://www.vox.com/2018/8/16/17692700/azealia-banks-elon-musk-grimes-explained|archive-date=November 11, 2018|url-status=live}}</ref> In May 2020, Grimes gave birth to their son.<ref>{{cite news|last=Kiefer|first=Halle|title=Grimes and Elon Musk's Baby Has Arrived, Just As Legend Foretold|date=May 4, 2020|url=https://www.vulture.com/2020/05/elon-musk-and-grimes-welcome-first-baby-together.html|work=Vulture|access-date=May 5, 2020|url-access=limited|archive-date=May 5, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200505021026/https://www.vulture.com/2020/05/elon-musk-and-grimes-welcome-first-baby-together.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|last=Trepany|first=Charles|title=Elon Musk shares first photo of his and Grimes' new baby boy: 'Mom and baby all good'|date=May 5, 2020|url=https://eu.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2020/05/05/elon-musk-grimes-welcome-baby/3082615001/|work=USA Today|access-date=May 5, 2020|archive-date=May 29, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200529124947/https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2020/05/05/elon-musk-grimes-welcome-baby/3082615001/|url-status=live}}</ref> Musk and Grimes originally gave the baby the name "X Æ A-12", which would have violated California regulations as it contained characters that are not in the modern English alphabet,<ref>{{cite news |last1=Schwedel |first1=Heather |title=What Does Elon Musk and Grimes' Baby Name Actually Mean? |url=https://slate.com/human-interest/2020/05/elon-musk-grimes-baby-name.html |access-date=May 5, 2020 |work=Slate|date=May 5, 2020 |archive-date=May 24, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200524150019/https://slate.com/human-interest/2020/05/elon-musk-grimes-baby-name.html |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|last=Lerman|first=Rachel|date=May 8, 2020|title=Elon Musk's baby name isn't just weird, it may be against California regulations|url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2020/05/08/musk-grimes-baby-name/|newspaper=The Washington Post| access-date=January 11, 2021|archive-date=December 31, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201231225820/https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2020/05/08/musk-grimes-baby-name/|url-status=live}}</ref> which they then changed to "X Æ A-Xii".<ref>{{Cite news|title=Elon Musk and Grimes have changed their baby's name. A bit|first=Jack|last=Guy|url=https://www.cnn.com/2020/05/25/entertainment/grimes-musk-baby-name-tweak-scli-intl/index.html|publisher=CNN| date=May 25, 2020|access-date=May 25, 2020|archive-date=May 25, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200525204407/https://www.cnn.com/2020/05/25/entertainment/grimes-musk-baby-name-tweak-scli-intl/index.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="xaea-xii.cnet">{{cite news|last=Cooper|first=Gael Fashingbauer|date=June 16, 2020|title=Elon Musk and Grimes saved a surprise for son X Æ A-12's birth certificate|url=https://www.cnet.com/news/elon-musk-and-grimes-saved-a-surprise-for-son-x-ae-a-12s-birth-certificate/|publisher=CNET| access-date=June 17, 2020|archive-date=June 17, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200617021513/https://www.cnet.com/news/elon-musk-and-grimes-saved-a-surprise-for-son-x-ae-a-12s-birth-certificate/|url-status=live}}</ref> They have received criticism for choosing a name perceived to be impractical and difficult to pronounce.<ref>{{cite web |title=Elon Musk and Grimes' newborn name X Æ A-12 'fails at the basic job of being a name,' says author |url=https://www.cbc.ca/radio/thecurrent/the-current-for-may-7-2020-1.5559171/elon-musk-and-grimes-newborn-name-x-%C3%A6-a-12-fails-at-the-basic-job-of-being-a-name-says-author-1.5559761 |access-date=August 12, 2024 |website=CBC Radio |archive-date=August 12, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240812165748/https://www.cbc.ca/radio/thecurrent/the-current-for-may-7-2020-1.5559171/elon-musk-and-grimes-newborn-name-x-%C3%A6-a-12-fails-at-the-basic-job-of-being-a-name-says-author-1.5559761 |url-status=live }}</ref> In 2021, they had a daughter via [[surrogacy]].<ref name="VultureBaby">{{cite web|first=Halle|last=Kiefer|url=https://www.vulture.com/2020/05/elon-musk-and-grimes-welcome-first-baby-together.html|title=Grimes and Elon Musk's Baby Has Arrived, Just As Legend Foretold|work=[[Vulture (website)|Vulture]]|date=May 4, 2020|access-date=July 19, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220310212753/https://www.vulture.com/2020/05/elon-musk-and-grimes-welcome-first-baby-together.html|archive-date=March 10, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="USATodayPhoto">{{cite web|first=Charles|last=Trepany|url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2020/05/05/elon-musk-grimes-welcome-baby/3082615001/|title=Elon Musk shares first photo of his and Grimes' new baby boy: 'Mom and baby all good'|work=[[USA Today]]|date=May 5, 2020|access-date=December 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230419161253/https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2020/05/05/elon-musk-grimes-welcome-baby/3082615001/|archive-date=April 19, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> According to Grimes, Go Won of the South Korean girl group [[Loossemble]] (with whom she collaborated in 2018) is her eldest son's [[Godparent|godmother]].<ref>{{Cite web|first=Palmer|last=Haasch|url=https://www.insider.com/grimes-x-ae-a-xii-baby-elon-instagram-loona-gowon-2020-5|title=Grimes says that X Æ A-Xii's godmother is a K-pop idol she collaborated with in 2018|work=[[Insider Inc.|Insider]]|date=May 26, 2020|access-date=July 19, 2022}}</ref>

Grimes and Musk "semi-separated" in September 2021.<ref>{{cite web|first=Devon|last=Ivie|url=https://www.vulture.com/2021/09/elon-musk-and-grimes-break-up-after-3-years-together.html|title=Elon Musk and Grimes Took the Red Pill and Broke Up|work=[[Vulture (website)|Vulture]]|date=September 24, 2021|access-date=September 24, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210924171854/https://www.vulture.com/2021/09/elon-musk-and-grimes-break-up-after-3-years-together.html|archive-date=September 24, 2021|url-status=live}}</ref> In January 2022, Grimes said of Musk: "I would probably refer to him as my boyfriend, but we're very fluid."<ref name="vanityfair surrogate" /> Despite fluctuating relationship statuses, in March 2022 Grimes described Musk as her "best friend and the love of my life".<ref>{{cite web|first=Christie|last=D'Zurilla|url=https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/music/story/2022-03-11/grimes-elon-musk-relationship-breakup-split|title=Never mind that new baby: Grimes and Elon Musk have broken up again, she says|work=[[Los Angeles Times]]|date=March 11, 2022|access-date=December 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230321012013/https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/music/story/2022-03-11/grimes-elon-musk-relationship-breakup-split|archive-date=March 21, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> In September 2023, it was reported that the couple had another son.<ref>{{cite web|author=Natalie Neysa Alund|url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2023/09/11/elon-musk-third-child-with-grimes/70822193007/|title=Elon Musk announces third child with Grimes, reveals baby's unique name|work=[[USA Today]]|date=September 11, 2023|access-date=December 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004104031/https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2023/09/11/elon-musk-third-child-with-grimes/70822193007/|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Bevan|last=Hurley|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/life-style/elon-musk-grimes-children-biography-b2408556.html|title=Elon Musk has secret third child with Grimes, biography reveals|work=[[The Independent]]|date=September 9, 2023|access-date=December 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231004101039/https://www.independent.co.uk/life-style/elon-musk-grimes-children-biography-b2408556.html|archive-date=October 4, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref> Later that month, Grimes sued Musk over parental rights to their children in a California court. Musk allegedly fought to keep the hearing closed, asking for the documents to be sealed.<ref>{{cite web|first=Matthew|last=Strauss|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-sues-elon-musk-over-parental-rights/|title=Grimes Sues Elon Musk Over Parental Rights|work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=October 3, 2023|access-date=December 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231003205426/https://pitchfork.com/news/grimes-sues-elon-musk-over-parental-rights/|archive-date=October 3, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|first=Brittany|last=Miller|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/life-style/grimes-elon-musk-sues-children-b2423577.html|title=Grimes reportedly sues Elon Musk for parental rights of their children|newspaper=[[The Independent]]|date=October 4, 2023|access-date=December 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231005135451/https://www.independent.co.uk/life-style/grimes-elon-musk-sues-children-b2423577.html|archive-date=October 5, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Naledi|last=Ushe|url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2023/10/04/grimes-petition-against-elon-musk-children-parental-rights/71054883007/|title=Grimes, Elon Musk kids' parental rights subject of court petition|work=[[USA Today]]|date=October 5, 2023|access-date=December 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231005044449/https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2023/10/04/grimes-petition-against-elon-musk-children-parental-rights/71054883007/|archive-date=October 5, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first1=Jack|last1=Newsham|first2=Grace|last2=Kay|url=https://www.businessinsider.in/tech/news/elon-musk-has-custody-of-son-x-despite-mother-grimes-objections-court-doc-says/articleshow/104384071.cms|title=Grimes doesn't want Elon Musk to have custody of their son, X. But he does, court doc says|work=[[Business Insider]]|date=October 13, 2023|access-date=December 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231013062236/https://www.businessinsider.in/tech/news/elon-musk-has-custody-of-son-x-despite-mother-grimes-objections-court-doc-says/articleshow/104384071.cms|archive-date=October 13, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>

From March 2024 to August 2025, Grimes was in a relationship with American DJ [[Anyma]].<ref>{{cite web|first=Lauren|last=Edmonds|url=https://www.businessinsider.com/meet-grimes-new-boyfriend-dj-anyma-elon-musk-custody-battle-2024-3|title=Grimes linked to new love interest DJ Anyma as her custody battle with Elon Musk continues|work=[[Business Insider]]|date=March 24, 2024|access-date=March 17, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324193051/https://www.businessinsider.com/meet-grimes-new-boyfriend-dj-anyma-elon-musk-custody-battle-2024-3|archive-date=March 24, 2024|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|first=Escher|last=Walcott|url=https://people.com/grimes-debuts-new-relationship-with-dj-anyma-beauty-and-the-beast-8619604|title=Grimes Debuts New Relationship with DJ Anyma: 'Beauty and the Beast'|magazine=[[People (magazine)|People]]|date=March 24, 2024|access-date=March 17, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324113325/https://people.com/grimes-debuts-new-relationship-with-dj-anyma-beauty-and-the-beast-8619604|archive-date=March 24, 2024|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Daniela|last=Avila|url=https://people.com/grimes-anyma-break-up-after-year-of-dating-source-exclusive-11795484|title=Grimes and Anyma Split After More Than 1 Year of Dating — but Remain ‘Good Friends’|magazine=[[People (magazine)|People]]|date=August 21, 2025|access-date=August 24, 2025|archive-url=https://archive.today/20250824182448/https://people.com/grimes-anyma-break-up-after-year-of-dating-source-exclusive-11795484|archive-date=August 24, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> In early 2025, after [[Elon Musk salute controversy|Musk was accused of performing]] a [[Nazi salute]] during Donald Trump's second inauguration, Grimes denounced Nazism and the "far alt-right" under intense pressure from her fans.<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Gil|last=Kaufman|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/grimes-distances-self-elon-musk-nazi-like-salute-trump-inauguration-1235880430/|title=Grimes Distances Herself From Ex Elon Musk's Nazi-Like Salute During Trump Inauguration Event: 'I Am Not Him'|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|date=January 22, 2025|access-date=January 24, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250123035301/https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/grimes-distances-self-elon-musk-nazi-like-salute-trump-inauguration-1235880430/|archive-date=January 23, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Julia|last=Ornedo|url=https://www.thedailybeast.com/elon-musks-ex-grimes-addresses-his-very-evocative-salute/|title=Musk's Ex Grimes Addresses His Very Evocative Salute|work=[[The Daily Beast]]|date=January 21, 2025|access-date=January 24, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250122002031/https://www.thedailybeast.com/elon-musks-ex-grimes-addresses-his-very-evocative-salute/|archive-date=January 22, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|author=Kevin E G Perry|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/music/news/grimes-elon-musk-nazi-salute-trump-inauguration-b2683824.html|title=Grimes 'happy to denounce Nazi-ism' after ex Elon Musk's salute controversy|newspaper=[[The Independent]]|date=January 22, 2025|access-date=January 24, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250124010956/https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/music/news/grimes-musk-nazi-salute-trump-inauguration-b2683981.html|archive-date=January 24, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> In February 2025, she criticised Musk for bringing their eldest son, X Æ A-Xii, to public events after he was photographed and filmed in the [[Oval Office]].<ref>{{cite web|first=William|last=Vaillancourt|url=https://www.thedailybeast.com/grimes-goes-after-elon-musk-for-using-their-son-as-a-prop-in-oval-office-press-conference-with-trump/|title=Angry Grimes Knocks Musk for Using Their Son in Live Presser|website=[[The Daily Beast]]|date=February 12, 2025|access-date=February 12, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250212035549/https://www.thedailybeast.com/grimes-goes-after-elon-musk-for-using-their-son-as-a-prop-in-oval-office-press-conference-with-trump/|archive-date=February 12, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first=Corinne|last=Heller|url=https://www.eonline.com/news/1398005/grimes-debuts-new-romance-2-years-after-elon-musk-breakup|title=Grimes Debuts New Romance 2 Years After Elon Musk Breakup|work=[[E!|Eonline]]|date=March 23, 2024|access-date=January 24, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250120072446/https://www.eonline.com/news/1398005/grimes-debuts-new-romance-2-years-after-elon-musk-breakup|archive-date=January 20, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref>

